\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-INR may hold its ground as \uc2 RBI\uc2  turns hawkish\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2022\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 April 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee could hold its ground versus the strengthening U.S. dollar and even gain slightly versus Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peers on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's baby steps towards policy normalisation and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as expectations of foreign portfolio inflows.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  on Friday held the repo rate at 4% and maintained its accommodative stance but introduced a new tool which sets a higher floor for the interest rate corridor, signalling a nuanced move away from its ultra-loose monetary policy .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  prioritised inflation above growth for the first time in three years and raised its inflation forecast for the current fiscal year by 120 basis point to 5.7%, to better reflect actual price pressures. This should help restore its inflation-fighting credibility and support the INR.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $11.17 billion in the week ended April 1 - the steepest fall in two years - revealing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determined \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem INR volatility.\par \par \uc2 The higher possibility of state-run \uc2 Life Insurance Corp\uc2 's record IPO going ahead in April \{nL2N2VH0HN] and a merger proposal between two domestic financial giants will raise expectations of foreign portfolio inflows, which should support the INR.\par \par \uc2 With USD/INR likely to consolidate in 75.50-76.50 range within a broader 75.00-77.00 band, trading the range looks prudent.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Krishna Kumar is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own. Editing by Sonali Desai)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-4-14T03:46:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220411ei4b00c9p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
