o led to an overall increase in our non-interest expense.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The intangible assets (i.e., favorable leases) that were acquired through the merger of CBoP were amortized over their estimated remaining useful life. This amortization resulted in a charge of Rs. 1.0 million in fiscal 2019. There were no intangible assets remaining to be amortized in fiscal 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Income Tax\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our income tax expense, net of interest earned on income tax refunds, decreased by 11.7 percent, from Rs. 119.4 billion in fiscal 2019 to Rs. 105.5 billion in fiscal 2020. Our statutory income tax rate decreased from 34.94 percent in fiscal 2019 to 25.17 percent in fiscal 2020. Pursuant to the change in the statutory tax rate, we stated our deferred tax assets as of March 31, 2019 at the newly enacted rate by recognizing a charge of Rs. 11.2 billion in our income tax expense for fiscal 2020. Consequently, our annual effective tax rate was 28.8 percent in fiscal 2020 compared to 35.1 percent in fiscal 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table gives a reconciliation of the Indian statutory income tax rate to our annual effective income tax rate for fiscals 2019 and 2020:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                    Year ended March 31,  \par                                                                                    2019                             2020  \par Effective statutory income tax rate                                                                      34.94   %               25.17   % \par Adjustments to reconcile statutory income tax rate to effective income tax rate:    \par Stock-based compensation                                                                                 0.55                    0.51    \par Income exempt from taxes                                                                           