mprised of interest expense on deposits, infrastructure and premises expenses for operating the branch network and other delivery channels, personnel costs, other direct overheads and allocated expenses. The Bank's retail banking loan products also include loans to small and medium enterprises for commercial vehicles, construction equipment and other business purposes. Such grouping ensures optimum utilization and deployment of specialized resources in the retail banking business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale banking segment provides loans and transaction services to corporate customers. As discussed above, loans to small and medium enterprises for commercial vehicles, construction equipment and other business purposes are included in the retail banking segment. Revenues of the wholesale banking segment consist of interest earned on loans given to corporate customers, investment income from credit substitutes, interest earned on the cash float arising from transaction services, fees from such transaction services and profits from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and derivative transactions with wholesale banking customers. The principal expenses of the segment consist of interest expense on funds borrowed from other segments, premises expenses, personnel costs, other direct overheads and allocated expenses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The treasury services segment undertakes trading \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on proprietary account (including investments in government securities), \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and derivatives trading both on proprietary account and customer flows and borrowings. Revenues of the treasury services segment primarily consist of fees and gains and losses from trading \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and of net interest revenue/expense from investments in government securities and borrowings. Revenues from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and derivative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and customer flows are classified under the retail or wholesale segments depending on the profile of the customer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Segment income and expenses include certain allocations. Interest income is charged by a segment that provides funding to another segment, based on yields benchmarked to an internally developed composite yield curve which broadly tracks market-discovered interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Directly identifiable overheads are attributed to a segment at actual amounts incurred. Indirect shared costs, principally corporate office expenses, are generally allocated to each segment on the basis of area occupied, number of staff, volume and nature of transactions. Wholesale banking segment includes unallocated tax balances and other items.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-6\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HDFC BANK LIMITED AND ITS SUBSIDIARIES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTES TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS-(Continued)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Summarized segment information for the years ended March 31, 2019, March 31, 2020 and March 31, 2021:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                           Fiscal year ended March 31,  \par                                                           2019                                          2020              \par                                                           RetailBanking                                 WholesaleBanking                     TreasuryServices         Total               RetailBanking                    WholesaleBanking                     TreasuryServices         Total          \par                                                           (In millions)                \par Net interest income/(expense) (External)        