\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, February 4\b0\par\par\uc2 1,338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2021\par 04:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access a PDF version of this newsletter, please click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_02042021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_02042021.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     Monetary Policy Committee\u8217\'20\'19s three-day interest rate-setting meeting\par continues in Mumbai.\par     Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nirmala Sitharaman\f28 \uc2 \f2  interaction with industry body \f28 \uc2 \f2 FICCI\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par members in New Delhi. \par     9:00 am: Budget session of Parliament continues in New Delhi.\par     10:00 am: Brookfield India Real Estate Trust IPO subscription continues in\par Mumbai. \par     10:00 am: Petroleum Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dharmendra Pradhan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , S&P Global Platts Ratings\par Chief Economist Shaun Roache, CRISIL Chief Economist Dhamakirti Joshi among\par others at S&P Global Platts webinar on South Asia commodities.\par     11:00 am: Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2  to inaugurate \u8216\'20\'18Chauri Chaura\u8217\'20\'19\par centenary celebrations via video conferencing.\par     11:15 am: Thermax management at an analyst call post 3Q earnings.\par     2:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 INOX Leisure\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a conference call post 3Q earnings.\par     2:15 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dinesh Khara\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a virtual press\par conference post 3Q earnings.\par     2:30 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a virtual briefing post 3Q earnings.\par     2:30 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  virtual press conference on 3Q results. \par     3:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apollo Tyres\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a conference call post 3Q earnings.\par     4:00 pm: Civil Aviation Ministry Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pradeep Singh Kharola\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a media\par briefing on Budget announcements pertaining to aviation in New Delhi. \par     4:00 pm: Health Ministry briefing on Covid-19 situation in New Delhi.\par     4:00 pm: Central Board of Direct Taxes Chairman Pramod Chandra Mody, Central\par Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs Member Vivek Johri at PHD Chamber post\par budget interactive session in New Delhi. \par     4:30 pm: Standard Chartered Bank South Asia Economic Research Head Anubhuti\par Sahay, DBS Senior Vice President and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Economist\f28 \uc2 \f2 Radhika Rao\f28 \uc2 \f2  at SYFX Treasury\par webinar on Budget 2021 and way forward.\par     5:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Godrej Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at an analyst call post 3Q earnings.\par     6:30 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a conference call post 3Q earnings.\par     \par     PROMOTION\par     LIVECHAT-REUTERS GLOBAL MARKETS FORUM\par     Reuters Journalists join Alastair Newton, Co-founder and director at Alavan\par Business Advisory, to discuss about global trade and investment. To join the\par conversation at 12:30 pm IST, click on the link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian services industry improved in January; job cuts continued\par     Growth in India's dominant services sector picked up in January as demand\par improved and consumer optimism was buoyed by the start of a huge COVID-19\par vaccination drive, although firms continued to shed jobs, a private survey\par showed on Wednesday.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SEBI bans Future CEO from securities market in insider trading case\par     India's market regulator on Wednesday barred Future Group Chief Executive\par Kishore Biyani and his brother Anil from accessing the securities market for a\par year after investigating insider trading in shares of its retail firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Future\par Retail\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 2017.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  posts first quarterly profit in nearly two years\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  swung to a quarterly profit on Wednesday and posted record\par revenue, as the Indian telecom carrier added more subscribers and saw higher\par data usage spurred by the coronavirus-led work-from-home trend.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian trade secretary stands by digital tax opposed by U.S.\par     India on Wednesday defended a new digital tax which faces opposition from\par big U.S. tech firms such as Alphabet's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the United States\par Trade Representative (USTR).\par     \u8226\'20\'22 WHO-led COVAX vaccine scheme agrees new supply deal with Serum\par     India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Serum Institute\f28 \uc2 \f2  will supply 1.1 billion doses of COVID-19 vaccines\par developed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 AstraZeneca\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Novavax\f28 \uc2 \f2  to the COVAX vaccine scheme as part of a\par new long-term deal, the head of the U.N. Children's Fund said on Wednesday.\par \par     \u8226\'20\'22 Hero sets up separate unit to sell Harley motorcycles\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hero MotoCorp\f28 \uc2 \f2  has set up a separate business unit to sell \f28 \uc2 \f2 Harley-Davidson\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par vehicles in India, Hero said on Wednesday, months after the U.S. company ended\par most of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the world's largest motorcycle market.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India tells \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2  to comply with order to block accounts -sources\par     India has told \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2  to comply with an order to block content alleging\par that Prime Minister Narendra Modi's administration was trying to wipe out\par farmers protesting against agricultural reforms, two technology ministry sources\par said.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian farmers to scale up protests as Rihanna weighs in\par     Indian farmers' leaders on Wednesday outlined plans to scale up months of\par protests against agricultural reforms, as their cause gained high-profile\par supporters in the West.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 'Reddit rally' stocks bounce on day after selloff, then dip after hours\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 GameStop\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other social media darlings rebounded in calmer trading on\par Wednesday from their sharp sell-off in the prior session as investors turned\par their focus to the possibility of tighter U.S. trading regulations.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Democrats push ahead on COVID-19 relief, Biden flexible on who gets checks\par     The Democratic-controlled U.S. Congress pushed ahead on Wednesday with a\par maneuver to pass President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $1.9 trillion COVID-19 relief package\par without Republican support, as the White House said it was flexible on a key\par element of the plan.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares drop as chip supply constraints hold back sales\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares fell in after-hours trading on Wednesday as the company said\par that semiconductor supply constraints that have roiled the industry were\par hampering its sales growth.\par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were trading 0.1% higher at 14,846.00.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is expected to strengthen against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par tracking the dollar\u8217\'20\'19s decline in the non-deliverable forward market. The\par pullback in Asian equities and possibility of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, would likely cap the rupee\u8217\'20\'19s upside.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian government bond yields will likely open marginally lower, as\par traders anticipate the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to announce bond-supportive measures\par tomorrow to bridge the demand-supply gap in the debt market. The yield on the\par benchmark 5.85% 2030 bond is likely to trade in a 6.05%-6.10% band.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Dow and S&P 500 rose slightly on Wednesday, registering a third\par straight session of gains, with Alphabet's shares hitting a record high\par following its strong quarterly results.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Japanese shares snapped a three-session rally on Thursday, mainly led by\par declines in chip-related shares as investors booked profits, while electronics\par and media giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped on upbeat third-quarter earnings.\par     \u8226\'20\'22  The dollar traded near its strongest in more than two months against the\par euro and the yen as pessimism about the U.S. economic outlook receded before the\par release of important data on the jobs market.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields rose and the yield curve steepened on Wednesday amid\par stronger economic data and a push in Washington to pass a massive relief plan to\par aid the coronavirus-battered economy.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil prices edged higher after the OPEC+ alliance of major producers stuck\par to a reduced output policy at a meeting on Wednesday, and as crude stockpiles in\par the United States fell to their lowest levels since March last year.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Gold and silver prices edged lower, weighed down by a stronger dollar,\par while investors awaited the passage of a massive stimulus package in the United\par States.\par     \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES    DEBT\par  PNDF spot         72.89/72.92  February 3       6,809.23    (199.12) crores\par                                                  crores      \par  10-yr bond yield  6.08%        Month-to-date    4,314       (254) crores\par                                                  crores      \par                                 Year-to-date     23,787      (2,772) crores\par                                                  crores      \par     (FII investment numbers are in Indian rupees. Source: National Securities\par Depository Limited)\par \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes                 \par     Stock market reports                \par     Non-deliverable forwards data              \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/intraday levels [IN SNAPSHOT]\par     Monthly inflows                      [INFLOWS RTRS TABLE IN]\par     \par     ($1= 72.83 Indian rupees)\par \par  (Compiled by Nachiket Tekawade in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-2-4T04:26:27.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210204eh2400gtn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
