\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, February 3\b0\par\par\uc2 1,238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2021\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access a PDF version of this newsletter, please click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_02032021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_02032021.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     Monetary Policy Committee\u8217\'20\'19s three-day interest rate-setting meeting begins\par in Mumbai. \par     9:00 am: Budget session of Parliament continues in New Delhi. \par     9:15 am: Home First Finance lists on exchanges in Mumbai.\par     10:00 am: Brookfield India Real Estate Trust IPO opens for subscription in\par Mumbai.\par     10:00 am: CBDT Chairman Pramod Chandra Mody, Joint Secretary Kamlesh\par Varshney at ASSOCHAM webinar on analysis of tax related budget proposals.\par     12:00 pm: Commerce Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anup Wadhawan\f28 \uc2 \f2  media interaction. \par     2:00 pm: Civil Aviation Ministry Joint Secretary Amber Dubey, Civil Aviation\par Security Director General M. A. Ganapathy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 FICCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  webinar.\par     3:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adani Enterprises\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a media conference call post 3Q\par earnings.\par     4:15 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adani Gas\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a media conference call post 3Q earnings.\par     4:00 pm: Brickwork Ratings Chief Economic Advisor M Govinda Rao at a webinar\par on decoding Union Budget.\par     5:30 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ramco Cements\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a conference call post 3Q earnings.\par     6:15 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adani Green Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a media conference call post 3Q\par earnings.\par     6:30 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Hotels Company\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at a conference call post 3Q\par earnings.\par \par     \par     LIVECHAT - REUTERS GLOBAL MARKETS FORUM \par     Reuters journalists will join Chris Rogers, Research analyst at Panjiva at\par S&P Global Market Intelligence, to discuss about global trade and investments.\par To join the conversation at 12:30 pm IST, click on the link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  scores Indian win as court freezes Future's $3.4 billion retail\par deal\par     An Indian court blocked Future Group's sale of a swathe of assets to rival\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised objections to the $3.4\par billion deal, in a battle of the retail titans that could reshape the shopping\par sector.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India's budget wins applause for keeping it real \par Indian Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's government is winning rare plaudits for\par having delivered a budget that is transparent and prudent, coming amid a\par coronavirus-led economic slump, despite a record fiscal deficit.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Wider fiscal deficits could pressure India's ratings, says Fitch\par     Wider fiscal deficits and a more gradual pace of consolidation will lift the\par Indian government's debt and pressure its sovereign ratings, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  said,\par cautioning that the fiscal firepower is limited due to a high debt ratio.\par \par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indigo Paints\f28 \uc2 \f2  soars in stellar market debut\par     Shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indigo Paints\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped in their market debut on Tuesday after a\par bumper response to the Indian paint maker's $160 million initial public offering\par (IPO) last month, underscoring investor confidence in the sector as the economy\par recovers.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India tells Sri Lanka to honour pact after Colombo takes back port\par contract\par     India said on Tuesday it expected Sri Lanka to honour its agreement to allow\par it to operate a major port terminal following Colombo's decision to pull out of\par the deal.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India's demand for COVID-19 drug remdesivir to fall, says Cipla\par     Drugmaker Cipla said on Tuesday that India's demand for COVID-19 drug\par remdesivir will likely fall in coming months, as daily coronavirus infections in\par the country continue to decline.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Verity Pharma and India's SII apply to distribute \f28 \uc2 \f2 AstraZeneca\f28 \uc2 \f2  vaccine in\par Canada \par     Verity Pharmaceuticals and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Serum Institute of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SII) have applied to\par distribute SII's licensed version of \f28 \uc2 \f2 AstraZeneca\f28 \uc2 \f2 's COVID-19 vaccine in Canada,\par potentially easing shortages as European manufacturing sites struggle to meet\par global demand.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil\f28 \uc2 \f2  may form subsidiary for retail assets to unlock value\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 IOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) could create a subsidiary for its retail assets to\par help unlock value, the head of finance at India's largest refiner said on\par Tuesday, a day after the government announced plans to monetise \f28 \uc2 \f2 IOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pipeline\par assets.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. Democrats take first step to go it alone on Biden's COVID-19 aid\par     Democrats in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday took the first steps toward\par advancing President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2 's proposed $1.9 trillion coronavirus aid plan\par without Republican support.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Japan's service sector slump deepens as COVID-19 emergency hits businesses\par     Japan's services sector shrank at the fastest pace in five months in\par January, as a heavy blow to demand from a resurgence in coronavirus infections\par and a state of emergency in parts of the country greatly hurt new business\par orders.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Bezos to give \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  reins to cloud boss Jassy as sales rocket past $100\par billion\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  founder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeff Bezos\f28 \uc2 \f2  will step down as CEO and become executive\par chairman, naming the head of its lucrative cloud computing division as successor\par in a sign of the company's transformation from web retailer to internet\par conglomerate.\par \par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were trading 0.3% higher at 14,777.50.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is expected to trade little changed against the dollar\par today amid a further uptick in most regional equity indexes and high probability\par of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian government bond yields will likely open little changed, as traders\par await likely measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the federal budget proposed\par higher borrowing. The yield on the benchmark 5.85% 2030 bond is likely to trade\par in a 6.10%-6.15% band.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. stocks finished sharply higher for a second straight day on Tuesday,\par helped by gains in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2 -parent Alphabet ahead of their results\par and by optimism over progress on a U.S. pandemic relief package.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Asian shares and U.S. stock futures rose as governments around the world\par looked poised to boost spending to help economies recover from the coronavirus\par and vaccine roll-out programmes accelerated.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The dollar traded near a two-month high versus the euro as investors\par looked to a widening disparity between the strength of the U.S. and Europe's\par pandemic recoveries.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields climbed on Tuesday and the yield curve steepened on\par supply concerns as Congressional Democrats were set to take initial steps to\par advance President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2 's massive COVID-19 relief plan.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil rose in early trade on expectations global oil stocks will fall back\par to more normal levels this year and as U.S. lawmakers moved closer to approving\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $1.9 trillion COVID-19 aid bill without Republican\par support.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Silver prices attempted a rebound after an over 8% plunge in the previous\par session prompted some buying, although the social media-driven rally that\par started last week appears to have cooled off.\par     \par     \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES         DEBT\par  PNDF spot         72.93/72.96  February 2       1,848.56 crores  133.51 crores\par  10-yr bond yield  6.13%        Month-to-date    (2,496) crores   (54) crores\par                                 Year-to-date     16,977 crores    (2,572) crores\par  (FII investment numbers are in Indian rupees. Source: National Securi