\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Thai baht hits 7-yr peak as investors see c.bank resistance slipping\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par 06:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Thai baht hits strongest level since late May, 2013\par     * Indonesia, Philippines cenbanks expected to hold fire\par     * S. Korea cuts growth outlook\par \par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Dec 17 (Reuters) - The Thai baht jumped to a more than\par seven-year high and breached a major resistance level on\par Thursday, as investors bet the country's inclusion on a U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  watch list might weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par determination to slow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains.\par     The baht firmed 0.6% to 29.83 per U.S. dollar. Thai\par exporters last week had called on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ensure the\par baht did not appreciate beyond the 30 per dollar mark, which is\par critical to keep them globally competitive. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it did not see a big impact on\par foreign trade and investment after the country was added to a\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monitoring list along with Taiwan and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     It added it had conducted two-way \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  only to ride\par out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility and had no intention of using the\par exchange rate to gain an unfair trade advantage. \par     "I think in the near-term the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might refrain\par from heavily supporting the baht due to the report ... by\par letting the baht dip below the 30 per dollar level today, it is\par a signal that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will let it move more freely in\par line with its Asian peers," said Poon Panichpibool, a market\par strategist at Krung Thai Bank said. \par     "The baht is going to be much stronger from now ... I don't\par think BOT will try to change that direction, but they will try\par to slow down the appreciation, such that exporters can hedge\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk."\par     The Taiwanese dollar climbed more than 1% against a\par broadly weaker U.S. dollar, with its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying the\par move was a reflection of the island's trade surplus with the\par United States. The Indian rupee rose marginally.\par \par     The Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso were\par steady ahead of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meetings later in the day. \par     Economists by and large expect both banks to leave interest\par rates unchanged after aggressive policy easing this year to\par support their pandemic-hit economies.\par     In equity markets, South Korea's KOSPI slipped 0.4%\par as the country reported a record daily jump in coronavirus\par deaths and cut its 2021 growth forecast. \par     Singapore shares shed about half a percent, after\par data showed the city-state's non-oil domestic exports\par unexpectedly fell 4.9% in November from a year earlier.\par \par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Indonesian 10-year benchmark yields are down 6.4 basis\par points at 6.037%\par     ** Top losers on the Singapore STI include: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting\par Singapore Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 1.69% at S$0.875; \f28 \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand\par Integrated Commercial Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 1.38% at S$2.15;\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corporation Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 1.17% at\par S$10.11\par     ** In the Philippines, top index gainers are \f28 \uc2 \f2 DMCI Holdings\par Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.16% at 6.15 peso, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Globe Telecom Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par up 2% at 2040 peso, \f28 \uc2 \f2 SM Investments Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 1.77% at 1094\par peso\par     \par     \par   Asia stock indexes and                                      \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0453 GMT                               \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2        INDEX  STOCK  STOCKS\par                        DAILY  YTD %                  S   YTD %\par                            %                     DAILY  \par                                                      %  \par  Japan                 +0.14  +5.10               0.15   13.28\par  China                 -0.07  +6.52               0.63   11.09\par  India                 +0.07  -2.91               0.27   12.75\par  Indonesi              +0.00  -1.49               0.32   -2.56\par  a                                                      \par  Malaysia              +0.27  +1.26              -0.53    5.27\par  Philippi              +0.15  +5.52              -0.61   -7.17\par  nes                                                    \par  S.Korea               +0.19  +5.91              -0.41   25.61\par  Singapor              +0.14  +1.30              -0.49  -11.30\par  e                                                      \par  Taiwan                +1.19  +6.99              -0.51   18.63\par  Thailand              +0.57  +0.27               0.62   -5.61\par  \par \par \par \par  (Reporting by Shriya Ramakrishnan in Bengaluru; editing by\par Richard Pullin)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12