\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, November 11\b0\par\par\uc2 1,045 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2020\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access a PDF version of this newsletter, please click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_11112020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://share.refinitiv.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_11112020.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     10:00 am: SIAM to announce October auto industry sales data.\par     11:30 am: ICICI Bank Executive Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anup Bagchi\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a conference call on\par the bank\u8217\'20\'19s mortgage business.\par     12:30 pm: HDFC Bank Country Head Payments Business, Consumer Finance,\par Digital Banking and Marketing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Parag Rao\f28 \uc2 \f2  at launch of \u8220\'20\'1CSmartHub Merchant\par Solutions 3.0.\u8221\'20\'1D\par     2:00 pm: Indirect Taxes Committee Chairman Bimal Jain at PHD Chamber of\par Commerce webinar on Goods and Services Tax.\par     2:30 pm: Bharat Forge conference call post second-quarter earnings.\par     3:30 pm: RITES Chairman and Managing Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rajeev Mehrotra\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a\par conference call post second-quarter earnings.\par     4:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTC India\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst conference call post second-quarter earnings.\par     4:30 pm: Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Telecom Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ravi Shankar Prasad\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par at the launch of a state-of-the-art office-cum-residential complex of Income Tax\par Appellate Tribunal in Cuttack.\par     4:30 pm: India International Exchange Chief Executive and Managing Director\par V. Balasubramaniam, HDFC Securities Chief Financial Officer Kunal Sanghavi among\par others at ASSOCHAM webinar on pre-budget consultation for capital market.\par     5:00 pm: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gland Pharma IPO\f28 \uc2 \f2  subscription closes.\par     \par     LIVECHAT-REUTERS GLOBAL MARKETS FORUM\par Reuters markets correspondents discuss how markets reacted to election\par uncertainty and the outlook going forward. To join the discussion at 7:30 pm\par IST, click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.refinitiv.com/en/products/refinitiv-messenger/editorial-communities-financial-forums"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.refinitiv.com/en/products/refinitiv-messenger/editorial-communities-financial-forums}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Australia's FAR sells Senegal project stake to ONGC Videsh in 'bittersweet\par moment'\par     Australia's FAR said it will exit the troubled $4.2 billion Sangomar oil\par project off Senegal's shore, agreeing to sell its 15% stake to a unit of India's\par ONGC Videsh for $45 million.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India revives plans to offer incentives for 6 million tonnes sugar exports\par India has revived a proposal to get sugar mills to export 6 million tonnes of\par the sweetener by incentivising overseas sales in the 2020/21 season, the third\par year in a row, as part of efforts to cut surplus stocks and prop up local\par prices, two government sources said.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  takes down underwear, doormat listings with Hindu symbols after\par India backlash\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday it had taken down listings of products such as briefs\par and doormats with Hindu sacred symbols, which were being sold on its overseas\par websites, following a furore on social media in India.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Dealers in India consider legal action against Harley Davidson \par Dealers in India for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Harley-Davidson\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday they are exploring legal\par action against the iconic American motorcycle brand after it effectively exited\par the market as part of a broader restructuring plan.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Biden says nothing will stop transition as Trump vows new legal action\par President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday that nothing would stop the transfer\par of power in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  pursued lawsuits\par in several states in a long-shot bid to hold on to power.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Apple launches MacBook laptops powered by its own computing chips\par Apple on Tuesday introduced a MacBook Air notebook and other machines with its\par first central processor designed in-house for Macs, a move that will tie its\par computers and iPhones closer together technologically.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 ByteDance challenges Trump's TikTok divestiture order\par ByteDance, the Chinese parent company of video-sharing app TikTok, filed a\par petition late on Tuesday with a U.S. Appeals Court challenging a Trump\par administration order set to take effect on Thursday requiring it to divest\par TikTok.\par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were 0.3% higher at 12,691.50. \par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is expected to trade lower against the dollar amid\par speculation the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s upside is capped by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. \par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian federal government bond yields will likely open largely unchanged\par as traders await October\u8217\'20\'19s retail inflation print and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s special\par open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , due tomorrow, for further cues. The yield on the\par benchmark 5.77% 2030 bond is likely to trade in a 5.90%-5.95% band. \par    \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2  closed lower and the S&P 500 dipped slightly on Tuesday as\par investors sold off technology stocks that benefited from virus lockdowns,\par favoring sectors that have suffered most during the pandemic instead on hopes a\par COVID-19 vaccine will turn the economy around.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Asian stock markets gained, as news of a working COVID-19 vaccine seemed\par to inoculate investors against worry about surging infections in Europe and the\par United States, while the kiwi rose as traders thought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sounded\par upbeat.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The dollar fell as optimism about a coronavirus vaccine was offset by\par worries about how the drug will be delivered and by a surge of new infections in\par the United States.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields rose modestly on Tuesday, as the market consolidated\par the previous session's strong gains fueled by news of a potential coronavirus\par vaccine.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil futures rose after an industry report showed that U.S. crude\par inventories fell by more than expected as prices continued to be supported by\par news of successful trials of a vaccine for coronavirus.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Gold prices edged higher supported by hopes of more U.S. stimulus measures\par as surging COVID-19 cases threaten to hamper economic recovery, although\par optimism over vaccine developments limited gains.\par     \par     \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES         DEBT\par  PNDF spot         74.21/74.24  November 10      4,426.03 crores  881.85 crores\par  10-yr bond yield  5.92%        Month-to-date    15,874 crores    1,993 crores\par                                 Year-to-date     63,762 crores    (1,05,153) crores\par  \par     (FII investment numbers are in Indian rupees. Source: National Securities\par Depository Limited)\par \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes                 \par     Stock market reports                \par     Non-deliverable forwards data              \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/intraday levels [IN SNAPSHOT]\par     Monthly inflows                      [INFLOWS RTRS TABLE IN]\par     \par     ($1 = 74.28 Indian rupees)\par \par  (Compiled by Pathikrit Bandyopadhyay in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-11T04:20:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201111egbb00ent\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
