\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Rupee sees best week in 2 years as investors weigh Fed message\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2020\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: Foreign flows into Asian stocks \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3f2vwbA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3f2vwbA}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Rupee hits highest level since March 5\par     * Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain on lower U.S. rate prospects\par \par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Aug 28 (Reuters) - India's rupee rose for the fourth session\par in five on Friday as traders reported no sign of a return of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling, leading gains across Asia against the\par dollar following a landmark speech by U.S. Federal Reserve chief\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     There was some strength for the dollar overnight as 10-year\par U.S. bond yields pushed higher after Powell's message that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would allow inflation to run higher and do more to\par get it there in future. \par     But it struggled throughout the Asian morning and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par including the Singapore and Taiwan dollars, as\par well as China's yuan, all traded a third of a percent\par or more higher. \par     The rupee has been surging since Monday, when the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to halt its recent policy of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the market against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and hit\par its highest in nearly six months on Friday, on course for its\par best week since late December 2018. \par     Traders said they expected the bank to return to the market\par soon, however, in part to ensure it builds more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves,\par $60 billion to $535.35 billion so far this fiscal\par year.\par     "The RBI must have let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate to shatter\par the complacency but this may not be the case going forward and\par we might see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again coming into action," said\par Gaurang Somaiya, an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at Mumbai-based broker and\par trading firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Motilal Oswal Financial Services\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     The Indonesian rupiah took back early losses to trade\par 0.2% higher, while the Philippine peso also rose against\par the greenback.\par     The jump in U.S. bond yields, however, capped flows into\par riskier Asian assets, with yields on long-dated government bonds\par for Malaysia, Thailand and Indonesia\par  all higher. \par     Shares in Jakarta took a beating, as the country\par reported its biggest daily spike in coronavirus infections.\par     Singapore shares snapped two sessions of losses,\par boosted by gains in the heavyweight financial sector, while\par Malaysian shares moved little on better-than-expected\par export data.\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Thailand's 10-year government bond yields are\par up 6 basis points at 1.47%, while Indonesian 10-year benchmark\par yields are up 6.4 basis points at 6.873%\par     ** Top gainers on the Singapore STI include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore\par Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.75% at S$3.73, \f28 \uc2 \f2 SATS Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  up\par 2.39% at S$3, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Keppel Corp Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  up\u8203\'20\'0B 2.19% at S$4.67\par     ** Top losers on FTSE \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Kl Index\par include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hap Seng Consolidated Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 3.55% at 7.6\par ringgit; \f28 \uc2 \f2 PETRONAS Chemicals Group Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 3.27% at\par 5.62 ringgit; \f28 \uc2 \f2 MISC Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 2.84% at 7.54 ringgit\par     \par     \par   Asia stock indexes and                                    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0710 GMT                             \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       INDEX  STOCK  STOCKS\par                       DAILY  YTD %                 S   YTD %\par                           %                    DAILY  \par                                                    %  \par  Japan                +0.47  +2.41             -1.41   -3.27\par  China     <CNY=CFXS  +0.38  +1.38              1.51   11.50\par            >                                          \par  India                +0.55  -2.76              0.79   -4.26\par  Indonesi             +0.10  -5.16             -0.65  -15.28\par  a                                                    \par  Malaysia             +0.00  -1.94             -0.64   -2.77\par  Philippi             +0.38  +4.68             -0.63  -24.71\par  nes                                                  \par  S.Korea   <KRW=KFTC  +0.06  -2.36              0.40    7.10\par            >                                          \par  Singapor             +0.30  -1.26              1.22  -20.86\par  e                                                    \par  Taiwan               +0.52  +2.55             -0.53    6.10\par  Thailand            