\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-Rupee unshackled by RBI absence, more gains likely\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2020\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Aug 25 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's 1.2% surge on Monday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly broke with a recent pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a 74.50-75.50 range, should pave the way for the INR to catch up with its emerging Asian peers.\par \par \uc2 India's rising coronavirus toll, expectations of a drastic slowing in the economy and a deteriorating fiscal position have all contributed to the rupee being one of the worst Asia ex-Japan performers in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believed to be aimed at quelling volatility, has prevented the INR from appreciating despite buoyant global risk appetite and substantial foreign investor inflows. Estimates from ANZ analysts place RBI dollar purchases at $30 billion in the four months to July, according to a Bloomberg report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bloom.bg/2EmvEGc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://bloom.bg/2EmvEGc}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also appears driven by a desire to build a buffer and improve INR competitiveness as India strives to become a manufacturing base .\par \par \uc2 Since early July the RBI's support level for USD/INR appeared to have moved down to 74.35-50, in line with broader dollar weakness, from 74.90-75.00 previously. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's absence on Monday signals a lower tolerance threshold now, with India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at record highs.\par \par \uc2 The immediate target for the USD/INR drop is 73.62-65, with rallies to 74.50-60 a selling opportunity.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Krishna Kumar is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-28T03:43:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200825eg8p00etd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
