\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Rupee jumps as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  steps back, Asian stocks rally\b0\par\par\uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2020\par 07:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: Foreign flows into Asian stocks \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3f2vwbA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3f2vwbA}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * S. Korea, Singapore shares up more than 1%\par     * Indonesian rupiah hits over two-week high \par \par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Aug 25 (Reuters) - India's rupee opened around 1% above\par levels from a day earlier on Tuesday after traders reported a\par halt in a run of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at keeping the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak to support its stuttering economy.\par     Over recent weeks, banks have spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to backstop the export sector as the\par nation struggles to emerge from the world's third worst\par coronavirus outbreak. \par     The rupee, which is about 4% on the year, jumped\par from opening levels of close to 75 per dollar to 74.24 rupees in\par early trade. \par     "If not for the RBI\u8217\'20\'19s active \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to absorb the\par inflows, INR would have traded much stronger than current\par levels," Australian bank ANZ said in a note to clients after the\par moves on Monday. \par     "The RBI will likely continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  though\par potentially not by as much as before, allowing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par appreciate into year-end."\par     Elsewhere in Asia, stock markets were mostly higher as signs\par of progress in U.S.-China trade negotiations bolstered risk\par appetite, with export-focused markets leading the way after\par Washington and Beijing said both sides saw progress in\par discussions over their phase 1 trade deal.\par     South Korea's KOSPI jumped as much as 1.5% and the\par won rose 0.3% against the dollar, with sentiment also\par supported by a slowdown in domestic daily COVID-19 infections\par from a peak of 397 reported on Sunday.\par     Taiwan and Singapore shares gained about 1%\par each, while Thai shares were 0.3% firmer. \par     In Indonesia, the rupiah advanced as much as 0.5% to\par a more than two-week high ahead of a bond auction later in the\par day, where the country's finance ministry aims to raise 20\par trillion rupiah ($1.37 billion) to fund its 2020 state budget.\par     "We expect demand for Indonesia government bonds to stay\par robust," said Duncan Tan, an interest rates strategist at DBS. \par     "The recent plunge in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -hedging costs also allows foreign\par bond investors to cheaply hedge the direct IDR exposure, and\par should be helpful to draw back in investors who may be concerned\par about IDR underperformance." \par     Indonesian debt has been a favourite with foreign investors\par over the years due to their attractive yields, the highest in\par Southeast Asia. \par     But investors have preferred to stay at the shorter end of\par the curve recently, pushing the spread between five-year\par  and ten-year debt to its widest since\par 2013.\par     "There is likely some amount of worries of higher inflation\par on the back of an expected expansion of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's balance\par sheet," Tan said, adding that more liquidity is also being\par directed to shorter-tenor bonds.\par     Shares in Jakarta were up about 0.8%.\par     Malaysian shares bucked the trend, dragged down by\par losses for its medical glove makers as progress on coronavirus\par vaccines and treatments dented the appeal of the sector. \par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Indonesian 10-year benchmark yields are down\par 0.7 basis points at 6.729%\par     ** Top gainers on the Singapore STI include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore\par Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 4.62% at S$3.85, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capitaland Mall Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  up 2.66% at S$1.93, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jardine Cycle & Carriage Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  up \u8203\'20\'0B 2.59% at S$19.4\par     ** Top losers on FTSE \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Kl Index\par include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hartalega Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 5.49% at 16.54\par ringgit; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Top Glove Corporation Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 5.23% at 26.46\par ringgit;\par     \par     \par   Asia stock indexes and                                    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0410 GMT                             \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       INDEX  STOCK  STOCKS\par                       DAILY  YTD %                 S   YTD %\par                           %                    DAILY  \par                                                    %  \par  Japan                +0.00  +2.49              1.85   -1.04\par  China     <CNY=CFXS  +0.14  +0.78             -0.19   10.79\par            >                                          \par  India                 0.00  -3.94              0.41   -5.38\par  Indonesi             +0.27  -5.13         