\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-RBI deftly guides USD/INR into a lower range\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2020\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 July 9 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  appears to have recently orchestrated a slightly lower trading range for the U.S. dollar versus the Indian rupee via suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The performance of China's yuan might explain why.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely perceived to have boxed USD/INR into a broad 74.90-76.30 range in May and June. But since early July the lower parameter of the RBI's tolerance level seems to have shifted to 74.35-50, in line with broader dollar weakness.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's reluctance to allow more meaningful INR appreciation despite buoyant global risk appetite and substantial foreign investor inflows marks a departure from its stated \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb extreme volatility.\par \par \uc2 But viewed in relation to the Chinese yuan's stability since April, it makes perfect sense. India is keen to attract companies seeking manufacturing sites outside China after the coronavirus pandemic disrupted global supply chains. Hence, the authorities are likely to favour INR stability - if not weakness - versus the CNY to maintain competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's dollar buying also creates liquidity and builds up needed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves given India's current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's 0.8% appreciation against the dollar since July 1 will provide the RBI some leeway to allow INR appreciation. But a sustained move beyond 74.35, the March 27 rupee high, is unlikely unless accompanied by significant yuan strength.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Krishna Kumar is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-7-12T03:46:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200709eg7900gfp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
