\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, June 16\b0\par\par\uc2 1,180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2020\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access a PDF version of this newsletter, please click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_06162020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_06162020.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     3:00 pm: ASSOCHAM webinar to discuss impact of COVID-19 driven lockdown on\par non-banking finance sector in Mumbai.\par     \par     PROMOTION \par     LIVECHAT - REUTERS GLOBAL MARKETS FORUM\par     Chris Weston, Head of Research at Pepperstone in Sydney, joins us to discuss\par the equity market rally, how much of the second wave of COVID-19 is a worry for\par the markets, and what to expect from here. To join the conversation at 9:30 am\par IST, click on the link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Election-bound Bihar state records nearly double national jobless rate\par     India's eastern Bihar state, one of the country's largest and poorest\par states, posted a steep rise in unemployment in the year ended June 2019 to\par record nearly double the national jobless rate, only months out from elections.\par \par     \u8226\'20\'22 RBI may need to choose between \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bond \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in H2-economists\par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market have\par helped reserves climb to a record $501.7 billion in early June, but economists\par say the pace of increase is likely to taper in the second half of this fiscal\par year.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors\f28 \uc2 \f2  to shed 1,100 JLR jobs after pandemic hits earnings\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to shed about 1,100 temporary jobs at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jaguar Land Rover\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par after it raised the cost-cutting target at its luxury unit by 1 billion pounds\par to ride out the disruptions caused by the coronavirus outbreak.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian exports fall by over 36% in May\par India's merchandise exports shrank by more than a third in May from a year ago,\par dragged down by a fall in global demand and shipments due to the outbreak of\par coronavirus, trade ministry data showed on Monday.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lakshmi Vilas Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  approached by potential investor\par     Indian private lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lakshmi Vilas Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Monday it had been\par approached by Clix Capital but gave no details after local media reported that\par the finance company had proposed taking a significant stake in LVB.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Criticism mounts as New Delhi hospital beds run out amid COVID-19 surge\par     India's capital is fast running out of hospital beds amid a surge in\par coronavirus cases and is struggling to contain the pandemic, after critics said\par it did too little to prepare and reopened shopping malls and temples too soon.\par [nL4N2DS21O\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India steps up bet on gas with first gas trading exchange\par     India on Monday launched its first gas trading exchange, enabling local and\par foreign players such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shell\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Vitol and Trafigura to sell directly to domestic\par customers.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Sweden's Sinch to buy India's ACL Mobile for $70 million\par     Fast-growing Swedish cloud computing services provider Sinch said on Monday\par it had agreed to buy Indian firm ACL Mobile for about $70 million in cash, its\par third large acquisition since the start of March.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Dutch Tata Steel employees hold further strike actions\par     Dutch Tata Steel employees held further strike actions on Monday to protest\par against job cuts planned as part of a broader restructuring, the FNV union said.\par \par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  keeps policy steady, eyes recovery from pandemic \par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept monetary settings steady on Tuesday and stuck to its view\par that the economy will gradually recover from the coronavirus pandemic,\par signalling that it has taken enough steps to support growth for now.\par  \par     \u8226\'20\'22 Beijing puts fresh curbs to stop spread of coronavirus out of Chinese\par capital\par     Beijing authorities imposed more restrictions to stop the spread of a fresh\par outbreak of coronavirus in the Chinese capital to other provinces, banning\par outbound travel of high-risk people and suspending some transportation services\par out of the city.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Fed will begin purchasing corporate bonds on Tuesday\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it will start purchasing corporate bonds on Tuesday\par through the secondary market corporate credit facility (SMCCF), one of several\par emergency facilities recently launched by the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to improve\par market functioning in the wake of the coronavirus pandemic.\par     \par     \par     Thomson Reuters/\f28 \uc2 \f2 INSEAD\f28 \uc2 \f2  Asian Business Sentiment Survey 2020Q2\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  and graduate business school \f28 \uc2 \f2 INSEAD\f28 \uc2 \f2  ask Asia-Pacific\par companies to rate their six-month business outlook, in a survey which in Q1\par yielded a sentiment index of 53 at near 11-year-lows. The latest survey will be\par released at 0300 GMT on Wednesday.\u8203\'20\'0B\par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were 1.8% higher at 9,992.00. \par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is likely to edge higher against the dollar as shares\par rebounded after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it will begin buying corporate\par bonds as part of a previously announced program to ensure flow of credit to\par large corporates.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian government bond yields are likely to open largely unchanged ahead\par of fresh supply of state debt, while market awaits steps from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to absorb excess supply. The yield on the benchmark 5.79% bond maturing in 2030\par is likely to trade in a range of 5.78%-5.82% today.\par    \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Wall Street closed higher on Monday following an announcement by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  regarding its corporate bond purchasing program that boosted\par investor confidence, which had been wavering amid a spike in new COVID-19\par cases.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Asian shares and Wall Street futures rallied on Tuesday as the formal\par start of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's corporate bond buying programme boosted global\par investor sentiment and calmed earlier worries about a second wave of coronavirus\par infections.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The dollar nursed losses on Tuesday, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par announced it would begin broad buying of corporate debt, boosting investor\par sentiment and appetite for riskier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields rose on Monday as stocks recovered from earlier\par losses and after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would expand its purchases of\par corporate bonds, boosting risk appetite.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil prices dippedon jitters that a rise in coronavirus infections around\par the world could hurt fuel demand, but hopes that production cuts could be\par extended kept declines in check.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Gold steadied supported by a weaker U.S. dollar, which fell after the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced it would buy individual corporate bonds in the\par secondary market, although an uptick in risk appetite limited bullion's advance.\par \par     \par     \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES     DEBT\par  PNDF spot         75.98/76.01  June 15          494.90       59.01 crores\par                                                  crores       \par  10-yr bond yield  5.79 pct     Month-to-date    23,335       (1,989) crores\par                                                  crores       \par                                 Year-to-date     (17,010)     (1,07,403) crores\par                                                  crores       \par  \par     (FII investment numbers are in Indian rupees. Source: National Securities\par Depository Limited)\par \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes                 \par     Stock market reports                \par     Non-deliverable forwards data              \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/in