\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, May 21\b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par 05:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access a PDF version of this newsletter, please click here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_05212020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_05212020.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://solutions.refinitiv.com/MNCIndiaSubscriptionpage}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     4:00 pm: Health ministry briefing on COVID-19 situation in New Delhi.\par     \par     LIVECHAT - CORONAVIRUS LOCKDOWNS\par     Dr. Jonathan Quick, managing director for Pandemic Response, Preparedness,\par and Prevention at \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Rockefeller Foundation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Professor of Global Health at the\par Duke Global Health Institute, and former director of essential medicines at the\par WHO, joins the forum to discuss strategies and risks as countries begin to ease\par coronavirus-prompted lockdowns. To join the discussion at 08:15 pm IST, click\par here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://refini.tv/2P8N0Wp}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 RBI may need to aggressively cut rates alongside fiscal stimulus -\par economists\par The Indian government's frugal economic stimulus package has put pressure on the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as analysts and economists say measures\par announced so far are unlikely to have any meaningful impact soon.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India to allow some domestic flights from May 25 - minister\par India will allow airlines to begin some domestic flights from May 25, its civil\par aviation minister said on Wednesday, two months after the country imposed a ban\par on air travel as it went into lockdown to curb the spread of the coronavirus.\par \par     \u8226\'20\'22 SoftBank-backed Ola follows Uber with job cuts as revenue sinks\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 SoftBank Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 -backed Indian ride-hailing company Ola will cut 1,400 jobs, or\par about 35% of its workforce, as it navigates a strict coronavirus lockdown that\par has halted 95% of its business, company chief Bhavish Aggarwal told employees on\par Wednesday.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Global coronavirus cases surpass 5 million, infections rising in South\par America\par Global coronavirus cases surpassed 5 million on Wednesday, with Latin America\par overtaking the United States and Europe in the past week to report the largest\par portion of new daily cases globally.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Japan exports fall most since 2009 as pandemic wipes out global demand\par Japan's exports fell the most since the 2009 global financial crisis in April as\par the coronavirus pandemic slammed world demand for cars, industrial materials and\par other goods, likely pushing the world's third-largest economy deeper into\par recession.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Fed debates longer-term crisis-fighting plan, minutes show\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  policymakers, still working to fully roll out a\par multi-trillion-dollar effort to shore up financial markets and an economy\par cratered by the coronavirus pandemic, last month dove into a new debate: how\par best to support the economy during a recovery they now agree could be slower and\par more fraught than initially thought.\par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were trading 0.8% lower at 9,018.25.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is expected to trade little changed against the dollar\par amid broad weakness in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on mounting U.S.-China tensions.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian government bond yields will likely trade largely unchanged in early\par session, as investors await the announcement of an open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to absorb New Delhi\u8217\'20\'19s additional borrowing and boost market\par appetite. The yield on the benchmark 6.45% bond maturing in 2029 is likely to\par trade in a range of 6.00%-6.08% today.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The three major averages on Wall Street notched their fourth gain in five\par sessions on Wednesday as investors again bet on a swift economic recovery from\par coronavirus-driven lockdowns and the potential for more stimulus measures from\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The dollar nursed broad losses and riskier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held gains as\par investors looked to a bright recovery from the COVID-19 pandemic, shrugging off\par diabolical forecasts and rising Sino-U.S. tension.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields slipped on Wednesday after a somewhat underwhelming\par debut of the first 20-year bond in decades left the market uncertain how the new\par government financing tool will fit in.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil prices edged higher after data showed U.S. crude inventories fell\par again, easing concern about a supply glut, though lingering fears over the\par global economic fallout from the COVID-19 pandemic capped gains.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Gold eased, as equities gained on hopes for a swift recovery from the\par coronavirus-induced economic slump, although losses were capped by optimism over\par further stimulus measures.\par     \par     \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES         DEBT\par  PNDF spot         75.81/75.84  May 20           (1334.16) crore  (883.69) crore\par  10-yr bond yield  6.04 pct     Month-to-date    10,996 crore     (20,290) crore\par                                 Year-to-date     (43,918) crore   (1,02,769) crore\par  \par     \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes                 \par     Stock market reports                \par     Non-deliverable forwards data              \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/intraday levels [IN SNAPSHOT]\par     Monthly inflows                      [INFLOWS RTRS TABLE IN]\par     \par     ($1 = 75.53 Indian rupees)\par  \par \par  (Compiled by Yoganand KN in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-21T04:15:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200521eg5l00d9t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
