 an investment trust company within the meaning of Section 1158 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.       Financial Statements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The financial information for the six months ended 31st March 2019 and 2018 has not been audited or reviewed by the Company's auditors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The financial information contained in these half year financial statements does not constitute statutory accounts as defined in Section 434 of the Companies Act 2006.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The information for the Company for the year ended 30th September 2018 has been extracted from the latest published audited financial statements. Those financial statements have been delivered to the Registrar of Companies and included the report of the auditors which was unqualified and did not contain a statement under either Section 498(2) or 498(3) of the Companies Act 2006. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.       Accounting policies \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The financial statements have been prepared in accordance with International Financial Reporting Standards ('IFRS'), which comprise standards and interpretations approved by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Accounting Standards Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  to the extent that they have been adopted by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Where presentational guidance set out in the Statement of Recommended Practice (the 'SORP') for investment trusts issued by \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Association of Investment Companies\f28 \uc2 \f2  in November 2014 and updated in February 2018 is consistent with the requirements of IFRS, the financial statements have been prepared on a basis compliant with the recommendations of the SORP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The accounting policies applied to this condensed set of financial statements are consistent with those applied in the financial statements for the year ended 30th September 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Indian Investmen