\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  more in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  forwards vs spot in Sept\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2018\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more actively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives market than the spot market in September, as it aimed to stem a sharp fall in the rupee and avoid tightening cash conditions in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Data released on Thursday showed the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  sold $7.09 billion in the forward dollar-rupee market in September, the highest monthly sales this year, compared with $4.95 billion in August. This is the second straight month for the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in the derivatives market than spot.\par \par \uc2 In the spot exchange rate market, the RBI sold a net $31 million in September, compared with $2.32 billion in August, data showed. In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the RBI's net outstanding sales stood at $1.27 billion, compared with $1.14 billion in August.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has declined about 11 percent since the start of the year, making it the worst performer in Asia, stung by high oil prices and large foreign dollar outflows.\par \par \uc2 However, the pace of fall has slowed as oil prices eased. The rupee lost 2.1 percent in September, compared with a drop of 3.6 percent in August, the worst since August 2015. In October, the rupee weakened by about 2 percent, while so far in November the pace of fall further slowed to 0.4 percent, according to Refinitiv data. The rupee ended at 71.9750 to the dollar on Thursday, compared with 72.30 on Wednesday. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-11-15T13:55:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181115eebf029el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
