\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, October 12\b0\par\par\uc2 996 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2018\par 05:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access the newsletter, click on the link:\par  \par  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_10122018.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_10122018.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par If you would like to receive this newsletter via email, please register at: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/india-morning/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/india-morning/}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     5:30 pm: Government to release August Industrial production data in New\par Delhi\par     5:30 pm: Government to release September consumer price inflation data in\par New Delhi\par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 TCS forecasts double-digit revenue growth after record profit\par     India's top software services exporter \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Consultancy Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  has\par forecast double-digit revenue growth in this fiscal year, driven by strong\par demand for digital services and healthy spending by key clients.\par         \u8226\'20\'22 Top brewers raided by Indian watchdog in price-fixing probe -sources\par India's antitrust watchdog raided the offices of three top beer companies on\par Thursday as part of an investigation of price-fixing allegations, three sources\par with direct knowledge of the matter told Reuters.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 RBI changes tack on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , focuses on forwards market \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has changed tack in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy, increasing its participation in the derivatives market in relation to\par the spot market in an apparent attempt to avoid a cash crunch in the banking\par system.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Dassault says it picked Reliance of its own will for India jet contract \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dassault Aviation\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it picked India's Reliance Defence as a partner for a\par big military combat deal on its own, countering a French online media report\par that said the Indian government insisted on the firm as a condition of the\par contract.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 GRAPHIC-India's NSE index off to its worst start to October quarter in a\par decade\par     India's benchmark NSE index is off to its weakest start to the October\par quarter since 2008 after a global sell-off on Thursday further dented investor\par sentiment just as the Indian economy enters its peak-demand festive\par season.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Flipkart\f28 \uc2 \f2  confident of bumper sales season; says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  losing relevance \par Online retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Flipkart\f28 \uc2 \f2 , owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Walmart\f28 \uc2 \f2 , expects bumper sales during the\par annual festive season that just kicked off, as it boasts that U.S. rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par is losing relevance in India.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 India to raise import tariffs on electronic and communication items\par     India said on Thursday it will raise import tariffs on several electronic\par items and communication devices, in another move to rein in imports and bolster\par a falling rupee.\par \par         \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  warns trade friction, market turmoil to hurt Asian growth\par     Sustained trade tensions could slash Asia's economic growth by up to 0.9\par percentage point in coming years, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, urging\par policymakers in the region to liberalise markets to offset the fall in export\par sales.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Call 'em crazy, but Fed officials likely to keep raising rates\par     A stock sell-off, rising trade tension with China, slower global growth and\par verbal pressure from the White House are unlikely to dent the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's rate hike plans in an economy performing in line with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forecasts.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 China constricts capital outflows with eye on yuan stability\par     China's latest attempts at restricting outward investment by its residents\par show just how nervous policymakers in the world's second largest economy are\par about possible capital flight spurred by a broadening Sino-U.S. trade war.\par \par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par     \u8226\'20\'22 SGX Nifty nearest-month futures were 0.3 percent higher at 10,312.50, from\par its previous close.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The Indian rupee is expected to open higher against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par after inflation in the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy trailed estimates, pulling the\par dollar index down by the most in two weeks.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Indian government bonds are likely to open higher today as a continued\par fall in crude oil prices eased inflation concerns, while the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par also expected to rise against the dollar. However, major gains in bonds are\par likely to be capped ahead of a fresh supply of notes and local retail inflation\par data. Yield on the benchmark 7.17 percent bond maturing in 2028 may trade in a\par 7.95 percent-8.02 percent band today.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Wall Street indexes continued their slide in Thursday's volatile session\par as investors worried about rising interest rates and braced for a trade war hit\par to corporate earnings a day ahead of the quarterly reporting season kickoff.\par \par     \u8226\'20\'22 Asian shares appeared tentative, holding steady after a nine-day losing\par streak, but sentiment was frail after Wall Street shares crumbled and\par expectations of market volatility shot up to an eight-month high.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 The U.S. dollar traded near its lowest level in nearly two weeks against\par its major peers as declining U.S. treasury yields and further losses on Wall\par Street soured sentiment.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields fell to one-week lows on Thursday, sliding for a\par second straight session, as Wall Street shares dropped a day after posting steep\par losses on worries about prospects for rising interest rates.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Oil prices steadied after a market rout driven by sharp falls in equity\par markets and indications that supply concerns have been overblown, but were still\par on track for a fall or more than 4 percent for the week.\par     \u8226\'20\'22 Gold edged down but held near an over two-month high hit in the previous\par session, when prices surged over 2 percent as a rout in global stock markets\par boosted the metal's safe-haven appeal.\par     \par     \par  CLOSE             FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES       DEBT          \par  PNDF spot         74.16/74.19      October 11     -$387.49 mln  -$273.18 mln\par  10-yr bond yield  7.99 pct         Month-to-date  -$1.83 bln    -$1.33 bln\par                                     Year-to-date   -$4 bln       -$8.08 bln\par  \par \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes                 \par     Stock market reports                \par     Non-deliverable forwards data             