\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  plunge as U.S. jobs data, Powell comments boost dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2018\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Amends headline, no change to text)\par     * EM Asia pressured by stronger dlr, U.S. yields\par     * Indian rupee hits fresh all-time low on steady oil prices\par     * South Korean won weakest in two weeks\par     * Chinese markets closed for the week\par \par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Oct 4 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on Thursday after\par robust U.S. economic figures and bullish comments from the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  boosted the dollar, prompting sustained regional\par outflows. \par     The greenback rose about 0.3 percent against a basket\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after news that U.S. service sector activity raced\par to a 21-year high in September. \par     It was further boosted when Fed chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par suggested that moving beyond neutral interest rates was a\par possibility. U.S. treasury yields were at multi-year peaks.\par \par     Khoon Goh, head of Asia research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Singapore said the mix of strong U.S. data and the Fed chair's\par comments bumped up the dollar and U.S. bond yields, putting\par downward pressure on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The prospect of a more aggressive Fed also rattled regional\par equities.\par     The Indian rupee plunged as much as 0.64 percent to\par a record low of 73.813 against the dollar after hitting an\par all-time low on Wednesday. Indian equities fell about\par 1.6 percent.\par     Traders said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par curb the rupee's fall.\par      Indian bond yields spiked as prices fell.\par     The South Korean won shed around 1 percent versus\par to the dollar to its weakest in more than two weeks. Weaker\par long-term sentiment has weighed on the won, which is closely\par tied to China though Korea's electronics exports, which may be\par at risk from the Sino-U.S. trade war.\par     The Indonesian rupiah continued to decline, \par falling as much as 0.7 percent versus the dollar and at its\par weakest in more than 20 years.\par     Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor stressed the need to raise\par interest rates before the Fed to avoid "drastic" capital\par outflows in the wake of a heavily flagged Fed hike in December.\par     The comments raised the possibility of another Bank\par Indonesian rate hike before mid-December although it has already\par raised interest rates five times since mid-May.\par     Indonesia has a large current account deficit stemming from\par its oil imports.\par     \par     INDIAN RUPEE\par     The Indian rupee is the worst performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this\par year, having lost more than 13 percent. It has been continuously\par pressured this year by higher oil prices.\par     "Despite a stronger dollar, crude oil prices continued to\par remain very elevated, which is putting further pressure on\par current-account deficit \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that rely on oil imports,\par India and Indonesia specifically," said ANZ's Goh.   \par     "The rupee hit yet another record low today and in the near\par term, it doesn't look like there's any respite coming," \par     Oil prices stood around four year highs on Thursday. Higher\par prices have swollen India's current account deficit, which last\par stood at around 2.4 percent of GDP, in the April-June quarter.\par India imports more than two-thirds of its oil needs. \par     A plunging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may prompt the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  to\par hike interest rates for the third time since June when it meets\par on Friday. \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0521 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR                              \par  Change on the day                                      \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    114.410     114.53        +0.10\par  Sing dlr                     1.382       1.3795        -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.775      30.670        -0.34\par  Korean won                   1129.700    1119.2        -0.93\par  Baht                         32.650      32.35         -0.92\par  Peso                         54.390      54.18         -0.39\par  Rupiah                       15180.000   15070         -0.72\par  Rupee                        73.720      73.34         -0.52\par  Ringgit                      4.147       4.137         -0.24\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    114.410     112.67        -1.52\par  Sing dlr                     1.382       1.3373  