\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India cenbank defends 72 rupee/dlr mark strongly - dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2018\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates to add RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  details)\par \par \uc2 By Suvashree Choudhury\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, mounting a formidable defence of the 72 rupee to the dollar mark in a reversal of its light-handed approach in the last few weeks, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 After briefly slipping to 72.04 to the dollar in early trade, the Indian rupee stayed above the 72 mark for most of the day with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling dollars whenever the unit came close to the psychological level. It was trading at 71.91 to the dollar at 0714 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "It seems like they (RBI) have changed their strategy and is determined to not let the rupee fall below the 72 mark just like it was supporting it at 69," said one senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have suffered a rout on concerns of higher crude prices and tariff wars, and crises in Argentina and Turkey have raised worries of a cascading impact across financial assets.\par \par \uc2 The speed of the rupee's decline from 69 to 72 per dollar in 15 trading sessions since mid-August, with the RBI only mildly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had stumped traders and stoked speculation that policymakers won't stand in the way of further falls. That emboldened rupee bears and sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record low of 72.11 to the dollar on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the RBI has likely been selling dollars through both private and state-run banks on the anonymous \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading platform throughout on Friday, underscoring its intent to staunch losses in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily only when the other global conditions is stable, like when the dollar is soft globally," said a chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 "That will make their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effective than on days when all other emerging markets are falling." (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-7T08:19:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180907ee9700v92\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
