\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Bearish bets on Indian rupee, Indonesian rupiah at highest in years\b0\par\par\uc2 926 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2018\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Fear of emerging market contagion sours sentiment\par     * Indian rupee bearish bets reach a 5-year high\par     * Bets on the rupiah weakening at highest in 3 years\par \par     By Rushil Dutta\par     Sept 6 (Reuters) - Bearish bets that the Indian rupee will\par weaken rose to their highest level in five years over the past\par two weeks, a Reuters poll showed, as the unit hit fresh lows,\par while most emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reeled from dollar strength and\par trade tensions.\par     With the index measuring the U.S. dollar against a basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  up more than 3 percent this year, though\par slightly weaker on Thursday, investors in emerging Asian units\par were spooked by tensions around global trade conflicts and fears\par of contagion from recession-hit Argentina and Turkey. \par     Appetites for risky assets were further reduced by South\par Africa's economy also slipping into recession. \par     "With growing concerns about Emerging Market (EM) contagion,\par risk appetite for Asian assets may remain very selective in the\par near-term," \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore said in a note.\par     Traders say the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par multiple times to put a floor under the sliding rupee.\par     On Thursday, however, the rupee breached a psychologically\par important mark of 72.00 for the first time on lack of supply of\par dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     Concerns over India's trade deficit and inflation, due to\par high oil and commodity prices, have prompted several foreign\par investors to exit long positions in the rupee, which is Asia's\par worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, weakening more than 12\par percent against the dollar.\par     Worries over some economic fundamentals have also caused\par investors to cut their long positions in the Indonesian rupiah\par .\par     Bearish bets on the rupiah piled up in the past two weeks\par and reached their highest since September 2015, the poll of 11\par respondents showed. That came despite attempts by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\par (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 to shore up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , among\par other measures.\par      BI has also raised policy rates four times since May, by a\par total of 1.25 percentage points.\par     On Thursday, Indonesia's finance minister raised import\par taxes on over 1,000 goods, ranging from cosmetics to cars, to\par cut imports and support the rupiah.\par     The rupiah, which was 0.2 percent stronger against the\par dollar on Thursday afternoon,  has fallen nearly 10 percent \par this year and has been hovering around levels last seen during\par the Asian Financial Crisis 20 years ago.\par     Investors were also more bearish on the Philippine peso, the\par survey showed, even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has raised its\par benchmark rate three times since May, by a total of 100 basis\par points, to try to tame inflation.\par     Philippine annual inflation hit a near-decade high in\par August, and raised the chances for a fourth rate hike soon. The\par next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting is on Sept. 27.\par     Meanwhile, bearish bets on the Singapore dollar\par remained largely unchanged, while those in the Chinese yuan\par  decreased marginally.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to increasingly\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the coming year if the\par dollar remains strong and trade pressures persist, a separate\par Reuters poll found.\par     The Reuters survey is focused on what analysts believe are\par the current market positions in nine Asian emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee\par , Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the\par Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3.\par     A score of plus 3 indicates the market is significantly long\par U.S. dollars. The figures included positions held through\par non-deliverable forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings ASIAPOSN are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par     \par  DDMM  CNY    KRW    SGD    IDR   TWD    INR   MYR    PHP   THB\par  6/9   0.92   0.64   0.86   1.37  0.68   1.72  0.90   1.13  0.24\par  23/8  0.93   0.71   0.84   1.27  0.91   1.19  0.88   0.86  0.47\par  9/8   1.52   0.94   0.80   1.21  0.99   1     0.86   1.02  0.66\par  26/7  1.55   1.08   0.84   1.35  1.13   1.25  0.76   1.44  0.87\par  12/7  1.00   0.91   0.68   1.31  0.88   1.18  0.64   1.35  0.70\par  28/6  1.28   1.03   0.94   1.32  1.03   1.43  0.94   1.58  0.73\par  31/5  -0.15  -0.17  0.39   1.06  0.33   1.42  0.69   1.25  0.06\par  17/5  -0.28  -0.33  0.28   1.08  0.07   1.31  0.21   0.68  -0.14\par  3/5   -0.23  -0.38  -0.08  0.56  0.04   1.11  