\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  drop; Indonesia,  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbanks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2018\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Rupiah sees 'decisive' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank appears to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to help rupee - traders\par     * Philippine peso rises after inflation at 9-year high\par \par  (Adds details on stock markets, capital outflows, updates\par numbers)\par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Sept 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Wednesday as fears of contagion from Argentina and other\par emerging markets buffeted the region, although suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  put a floor under the Indonesian rupiah and\par the Indian rupee.\par     Stock markets fell across the region and the safe-haven\par dollar hovered near a two-week high as heightened worries\par over international trade conflicts and emerging market weakness\par curbed investors' appetite for riskier assets.\par     Risk appetite for emerging market assets was further soured\par after South Africa's economy fell into recession, joining Turkey\par and Argentina. The Turkish lira and Argentinean peso extended\par losses.\par     Indonesian stocks fell as much as 4.8 percent -- their\par biggest one-day loss in at least five years-- while Philippine\par stocks sank more than 2 percent at one point.   \par     Investors were also wary about the prospect of fresh U.S\par tariffs on another $200 billion of Chinese goods that could be\par unveiled after a public comment period on such a proposal ends\par on Thursday. Market participants also awaited key U.S. payroll\par data later in the week.\par     "At this point there's still further pressure on emerging\par markets generally, and markets are awaiting two key events- one\par is the U.S. payrolls numbers and secondly whether or not the\par U.S. will announce the tariffs when the consultation period\par ends," said Khoon Goh, ANZ's Singapore-based head of Asia\par research.\par     The Philippine peso, which has fallen against the\par dollar the past five days, rose about 0.12 percent, in contrast\par to the country's stocks.\par     The annual inflation rate quickened at its fastest in more\par than nine years in August, implying that a fourth interest rate\par hike by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be on the cards.\par \par     The country has been struggling to contain inflation, as\par well as a large current account deficit.\par     The Malaysian ringgit fell 0.14 percent to the dollar\par and touched its lowest level since November 2017 as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its benchmark interest rate steady at a meeting on\par Wednesday, as expected.\par     Malaysian exports grew more than expected in July on higher\par shipments to China and increased demand for manufactured goods.\par \par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The Indonesian rupiah hovered around levels last\par seen during the Asian financial crisis two decades ago.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it had "decisively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond markets on Wednesday to curb\par volatility. \par     Thanks to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , "we have a stable rupiah today,\par but on the other side the demand for hedging is up, and there is\par already increased activity in the non-deliverable forwards (NDF)\par market," said Fakhrul Fulvian, chief economist at Trimegah\par Securities.\par     "It indicates that rupiah depreciation is likely to\par continue."\par     The rupiah has lost more around 1 percent over the past\par three days, after shedding more than 2 percent in August.\par     Indonesian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joko Widodo\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday that a\par priority was to increase investment and exports to contain the \par current account deficit, which has dragged on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par \par     The government also promised strict action against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par speculators, and announced plans to delay import-heavy energy\par projects in a bid to push up the rupiah.\par      At 0604 GMT, one-year rupiah NDFs were quoted\par at 16,251 per dollar, 8.9 percent weaker than the spot level. \par     The Indonesian equities market has seen outflows of $3.68\par billion so far this year as of Sept. 4. Indonesia saw net\par outflows of $2.96 billion in 2017, according to stock exchange\par data.\par     \par     INDIAN RUPEE\par     The Indian rupee fell 0.49 percent to the dollar.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  likely sold dollars at 71.80\par rupees in the local spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to stem the sharp fall,\par two traders told Reuters.\par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0723 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day      