\par\par \b \uc2 Indian shares track broader Asia lower; rupee hits fresh low\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2018\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * NSE index down 0.37 pct, \uc2 BSE\uc2  index 0.31 pct lower\par \par \uc2 * RBI likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support rupee - traders\par \par \uc2 * Sensex heads for 6th session of losses\par \par \uc2 By Chris Thomas\par \par \uc2 Sept 5 (Reuters) - Indian shares edged down in line with broader Asia on Wednesday, with banks and consumer goods stocks leading the losses, while the rupee fell to a fresh low as simmering trade tensions continued to hurt emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stock markets in Asia tracked global peers lower as heightened worries over international trade conflicts curbed investor appetite for riskier assets. MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan was down over 1 percent as of 0529 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee fell to a new low of 71.8 against the dollar on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  mildly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday, two traders told Reuters, to ease the pressure on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, markets at this point are very toppish. Not many people have valuation comfort at these levels. So, taking some money off the table is completely part of the course," said Tirthankar Patnaik, India Strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The NSE index had been on a record-setting run over the last two months, marking fresh highs 11 times in August alone. Meanwhile, the \uc2 BSE\uc2  index is Asia's top performing index this year, thanks to strong June-quarter earnings.\par \par \uc2 The broader NSE index was 0.38 percent lower at 11,477.15 as of 0608 GMT, on track for a third consecutive session of losses.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark \uc2 BSE\uc2  index, down 0.32 percent at 38,035.75, was headed for its sixth straight session of losses.\par \par \uc2 Hindustan Unilever Ltd\uc2 , down as much as 2.2 percent at a near 10-week low, was the biggest drag on the Nifty 50.\par \par \uc2 Coal India Ltd\uc2 , down 2.7 percent at a near five-week low, was the top loser on the index.\par \par \uc2 Heavyweight lenders \uc2 HDFC Bank Ltd\uc2 , \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank Ltd\uc2  and \uc2 ICICI Bank Ltd\uc2  fell between 0.7 and 1.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, gold financing company \uc2 Muthoot Finance\uc2  jumped 10 percent in its biggest intraday percentage gain since March 2017 after posting a 43 percent growth in June-quarter profit.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Chris Thomas in Bengaluru; Editing by Vyas Mohan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-5T07:40:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180905ee9500pb5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
