\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  strengthen; hopes pinned on U.S.- China talks\b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2018\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * China's yuan posts  biggest intraday gain in nearly\par 7-mnths\par     * Indian rupee at record low\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Chandini Monnappa\par     Aug 16 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened on\par Thursday, with the Chinese yuan leading the gains, after news of\par proposed Sino-U.S. negotiations sparked hopes of a trade war\par armistice. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Commerce\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday that it had\par been invited by the United States to hold trade talks with U.S.\par Under Secretary of the Treasury for International Affairs David\par Malpass.\par     News of proposed negotiations between Beijing and Washington\par lifted spirits in what has been a grim week for regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis spilled over into\par other emerging markets, compounded by weak macro-economic data\par from China.\par     The dollar index against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  was 0.17 percent lower at 96.536. It pulled back from a\par 13-month high of 96.984 scaled the previous day on demand for\par safe-haven assets. \par     China's yuan strengthened as much as 0.8 percent\par against the dollar, its best session in nearly seven months.\par     Prior to market opening, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the yuan's midpoint rate at 6.8946 per dollar,\par its weakest level since May 12 2017, and 90 pips weaker than the\par previous fix of 6.8856.\par     Indonesia's rupiah strengthened slightly to 14,595,\par pulling back from its weakest point in almost three years seen\par on Wednesday, after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised interest\par rates for the fourth time since mid-May as a defensive\par measure.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's intensified efforts come after the rupiah\par was battered this week by international political tensions and\par concerns about the country's widening trade deficit.\par     Indonesia reported on Wednesday a wider than expected July\par trade deficit of $2 billion, the biggest in five years and more\par than triple what economists expected, as the value of imports\par hit a record high.\par     Singapore's dollar strengthened 0.44 percent and the\par Thai Baht was 0.24 percent stronger\par     South Korea's won and the Indian rupee\par were the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region that weakened.\par     \par     The Indian rupee\par     \par     The region's worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, India's\par rupee weakened as much 0.6 percent to hit a record low\par as worries about a widening trade deficit soured sentiment. \par     The trade ministry said on Tuesday that India's trade\par deficit widened to 18.02 billion in July, its\par highest in more than five year highs, driven largely by a surge\par in oil imports.\par     Inflation remains a central concern for a country that\par imports 80 percent of its crude oil needs, so rising oil prices\par also weigh on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A senior finance ministry official said on Tuesday that\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not do much to\par stabilise the rupee after it plunged to record lows on Monday in\par the fallout from Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis.\par     "With an apparently shallow \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tightening cycle\par ahead, the current rupee depreciation trend looks to be a\par prolonged one," ING said in a note. \par     "The next challenge will be a string of state elections,\par which should see investors starting to add a political risk\par premium into local financial assets."\par     Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who is struggling to cap\par inflation, is expected to seek a second term in national\par elections in 2019. \par \par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0534 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.790     110.73        -0.05\par  Sing dlr                     1.374       1.3799        +0.42\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.842      30.858        +0.05\par  Korean won                   1127.600    1127.9        +0.03\par  Baht                         33.260      33.32         +0.18\par  Peso                         53.467      53.47         +0.01\par  Rupiah                       14575.000   14595         +0.14\par  Rupee                        70.195      69.90         -0.43\par  Ringgit                      4.097       4.102         +0.12\par  Yuan                         6.885       6.9340        +0.72\par  Change so far in 2018                              