\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cenbank likely  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to stem rupee fall - dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2018\par 09:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the rupee on Friday, after most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply on heightened global tensions, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell to as low as 69.03 to the dollar, its lowest since July 24, before trimming some of its losses to trade at 68.95.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like RBI might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sajal Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates at Edelweiss Securities.\par \par \uc2 "After the rupee opened with a gap, no one was willing to sell (dollars) at those levels. The rupee will continue to track the CNH. The next technical level for the rupee is 69.10."\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia so far in 2018, falling 7.4 percent since the start of January. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been beset by a host of factors, with higher oil prices adding to worries about inflation, current account and fiscal deficits and rising global trade tensions.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly in recent months to slow the slide, but it has still lost 3 percent since start of June.\par \par \uc2 With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiking interest rates, the rupee is expected to trade in a tight range in the coming year, possibly edging up to 68.22 but remaining near its historic low, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 The sharp fall in the rupee had prompted foreign investors to sell $5.35 billion in debt and equity in India. But flows turned mildly positive in July and August.\par \par \uc2 Since the rupee is traded over the counter, the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the day is difficult to ascertain. However, a few dealers estimated that the RBI might have sold close to $600-800 million so far on Friday to stem the rupee's fall.\par \par \uc2 The RBI typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through state-run banks.\par \par \uc2 Since April RBI has sold $21 billion in spot and $10 billion in forwards, according to traders and analysts, estimating from the fall in overall \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin data.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI can hardly do anything against such a massive (dollar) selling force. Even if it tries to contain the slide today, on Monday the rupee will once again be under pressure," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 "The next crucial level for stop losses to get triggered at is 70, with many options with sell calls at that level." (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-10T08:03:57.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180810ee8a00w3l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
