\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets Fight Back Against  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Slides -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2018\par 16:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1019 ET - Emerging-market central banks are tapping a roughly $6 trillion stash of foreign reserves as they struggle to contain deepening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declines. Emerging-market central banks used roughly $57 billion in foreign reserves in June, according to preliminary forecasts from research firm Exante Data, which would rank as the largest monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late 2016. Central banks in Brazil, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Argentina have been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent months, but their efforts have had mixed results. The Brazilian real is down 14% against the dollar this year, while the rupee is down 7% and the Argentine peso is down 34%. (chelsey.dulaney@wsj.com; @chelseydulaney)\par \par \uc2 0953 ET - The resignation of the U.K. minister responsible for overseeing the U.K.'s plan to quit the EU has increased the chances of Britain crashing out of the bloc or delaying the country's exit, says Daiwa Capital Markets. "The \uc2 UK government\uc2  looks to be in chaos," says Daiwa's \uc2 Chris Scicluna\uc2  . "Even if May continues to hold her position as PM, the noises from David Davis and key Brexiter backbenchers strongly suggest she would now fail to force through Parliament any final withdrawal agreement - which, even if it were based on Friday's Cabinet agreement, would still likely require further concessions to be made to Brussels. So the likelihood of a no-deal Brexit or Article 50 extension, and/or a new UK general election, all look to have increased." (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0950 ET - The U.K. is going to ask the \uc2 European Union\uc2  for the chance to stay in the single market for goods and agriculture, and to apply different tariffs to the EU . Where tariff rates differ, the U.K. would collect fees on the EU 's behalf. ING says "the EU will almost certainly say no" to these proposals. There could be practical issues of the U.K. collecting potentially higher EU tariffs. There are also concerns that different tariffs "could encourage smuggling." And the thought of a third country collecting EU tariffs is "reportedly unpopular in Brussels." Moreover, if the U.K. stays in the single market could be seen as cherrypicking and the EU "is worried that other countries could seek similar concessions." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0943 ET - \uc2 US government\uc2  bonds fall as the market prepares for the Treasury's scheduled auctions of three-, 10- and 30-year debt this week. The auctions follow Friday's Labor Department report which showed that the economy continues to add jobs at a steady clip, yet without producing the kind of pressure for higher wages that many economists have been expecting given the tight labor market. The yield on the benchmark 10-year Treasury note rose to 2.858% from 2.831% Friday. (daniel.kruger@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 ET - An acceleration in U.S. core inflation may feed through into eurozone government bonds, causing their yields to rise, even if there is no sign of eurozone core inflation picking up through the summer, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. "We could have a second-round effect from what happens in the U.S.," Mr. Nouen says, referring to U.S. core inflation having reached the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's 2% target. If core inflation increases again, it may make the Fed more inclined to raise interest rates further, lifting yields. This may in turn have a contagion effect on European government bond yields, he says. U.S. core price inflation, which the Fed follows closely, rose 2% on the year in May, Commerce Department data released end-June showed.(emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0938 ET - Improving purchasing managers' surveys on eurozone economic activity suggest long-term government bond yields in the region have potential to rise, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. "We think \uc2 PMI\uc2  data play a large part in the moves of long-term bond yields," Mr. Nouen says. "If there is a sign of economic rebound, with better \uc2 PMI\uc2  indices in the summer, it could lead to bond yields going higher," Mr. Nouen says. In 2018, the German 10-year Bund yield peaked in early February at around 0.77%, when the release of \uc2 PMI\uc2  data for January showed a peak for January, he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0938 ET - Economic models show that trade tariffs announced by the U.S. so far may not have much impact on growth but the effect on financial market sentiment will be important, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. Some surveys have shown that companies are starting to worry, which "may lead to some delay in capital expenditures," Mr. Nouen says. Trade tensions have come at a time when global growth is good, so the impact could be like putting sand into the machine: not enough to stop it but possibly causing a little slowdown in growth. "But if things escalate, we could have a bigger impact," Mr. Nouen says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0937 ET - In light of the Italian government's fiscal expansion plans, investors will be keeping a close eye on Italy's upcoming rating reviews, given the possibility of potential downgrades for the country, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. "The question is obviously how the budget will go down with the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  and how it will go down with the rating agencies," Mr. Nouen says. DBRS is scheduled to review Italy on July 13, followed by \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  on Aug. 31 and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Investors Service on Sept. 7 and S&P Global Ratings on Oct. 26. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0937 ET - Market fears over Italy's populist government have calmed for now, but investors remain wary over its plans for sizeable fiscal spending and these concerns could return to haunt markets in the autumn, says Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion. "I wouldn't say the market isn't worried," he tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. The 10-year Italian-German bond spread is still around 240 basis points, "still significant" and well above its pre-election levels, Mr. Nouen says. The 10-year Italian-German spread stood at 139 basis points on the last trading day before the March 4 election. While the Italian government clarified that it doesn't want to exit the euro, the budget is a concern given that "Italy has very little fiscal space," with a debt-to-GDP ratio around 130% and a "very low" trend growth level, Mr. Nouen says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0936 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's forward guidance that it will keep interest rates at present levels at least through summer 2019 and its commitment to reinvest maturing bonds may further encourage eurozone countries to issues ultra-long government bonds, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. Ultra-long bonds have a maturity of 15 years or longer. "We think the \uc2 ECB\uc2  will buy a significant part of its portfolio in long-term bonds," Mr. Nouen says. "These reinvestments will keep yields at a low level, it will make issuance at long maturities still interesting." Ultra-long government bond issuance in the eurozone has mushroomed in recent years as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's asset purchase program led to cheap funding.(emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0936 ET - The seasonal slowdown of government bond issuance in the eurozone in the summer is typically supportive of bond valuations. However, the seasonal pick-up of supply in the autumn is unlikely to weigh on bond prices significantly, Julien-Pierre Nouen, chief economist at Lazard Fr\u232\'00\'E8res Gestion, tells Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. Valuations shouldn't be impacted "because supply will be in line with what has been forecast at the beginning of the year," Mr. Nouen says. There is a little growth shortfall in the eurozone but that won't necessarily lead to a bigger deficit than currently forecast, Mr. Nouen says. The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's EUR45 billion asset purchase in 4Q and the prospect of EUR180 billion reinvestment in 2019 are "quite significant," Mr. Nouen says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0922 ET - A fall towards the June 14 low of 1.1563 in EUR/USD, the day of the last \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, could happen, says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  , but it will depend "on whether the return to calm waters for the remnibi and Chinese equity markets can endure." Also, it will depend on "how emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  respond to whether the U.S. moves ahead with the second tranche of trade tariffs." The remnibi has been falling massively on the past days, dragging down other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pushing the dollar up. But most of the EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are up against the dollar on Monday. For now, EUR/USD "almost entirely" recovered the losses of June 14, last trading up 0.3% at 1.1778 on Monday. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 09, 2018 10:19 ET (14:19 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180709ee79001ua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
