\par\par \b \uc2 India's rupee still over-valued by 5-7 pct - government adviser\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2018\par 13:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, July 3 (Reuters) - India's rupee is currently over-valued by 5-7 percent, a senior government adviser said on Tuesday, indicating that New Delhi is unlikely to support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shedding close to 7 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee fell to a record low of 69.0950 to the dollar on Thursday and was trading at 68.58 in late trade on Tuesday. It is the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia this year.\par \par \uc2 "The rate of inflation in India has been much higher than the global rate and that is what determines the real effective exchange rate," \uc2 Rajiv Kumar\uc2 , vice chairman of NITI Aayog, a government think tank, told reporters in New Delhi.\par \par \uc2 "And the real effective exchange rate today at 69 or 68.97 is still over-valued by 5 to 7 percent."\par \par \uc2 Kumar, who advises the government on economic issues and is on the board of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not necessary.\par \par \uc2 "There is no question at all of either getting worried, getting nervous or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," Kumar said, adding \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic growth was expected to pick up to over 8 percent in the next year from 7.7 percent in the March quarter.\par \par \uc2 He said India was not aiming to protect the rupee at any particular level and any RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at only containing volatility.\par \par \uc2 "RBI has always maintained and practised that they will never interfere directly in the market to protect the rupee at any particular level."\par \par \uc2 In a separate note, \uc2 UBS Securities\uc2  said on Tuesday the rupee was expected to remain in the range of 68-72 against dollar in the short term, on rising external risks, but added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control volatility.\par \par \uc2 "If external stress continues to rise and/or the USD strengthens, we believe policymakers could consider raising USD deposits as a last resort to stabilise the rupee," the note added. (Reporting by Manoj Kumar, editing by Raju Gopalakrishnan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-3T12:42:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180703ee7300f2h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
