\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rising U.S. yields weigh on most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 , rupee cuts losses\b0\par\par\uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2018\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * India's rupee pares losses after touching another over\par 1-yr low\par     * Indonesian rupiah falls, eyes on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meet on\par Thursday \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expected to stand pat on rates, baht down \par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Nikhil Nainan\par     May 16 (Reuters) - A surge in U.S. bond yields supported the\par dollar on Wednesday and knocked most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the\par Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah suffering the biggest\par losses.\par     A solid rise in U.S. consumer spending numbers sent long\par term Treasury yields surging to a seven-year peak of 3.095\par percent.\par     "There's permanence building as waves of fresh dollar longs\par hit the books," Stephen Innes, head of trading APAC at Oanda,\par said in a note, as the greenback hovered around a\par five-month high. \par     Denting risk was news that North Korea called off high-level\par talks with Seoul, throwing into question June's planned historic\par summit between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Jong Un\f28 \uc2 \f2  and U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par Pyongyang denounced U.S.- South Korean military exercises as a\par provocation. \par     "This will weigh on the Korean reconstruction beneficiaries\par that have had a strong run on peace and even reunification hopes\par recently," \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts wrote in a note.\par     The South Korean won fell 0.3 percent to 1077.2\par per dollar. \par     The Indian rupee recovered some losses following\par Tuesday's volatile session, as suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a second consecutive day stemmed the\par rupee's fall.\par      A senior dealer at a state-run bank, estimated that within\par the first 10 minutes the RBI might have sold $300 million to\par $400 million proactively to prevent any sharp fall in the rupee.\par     Some dealers had anticipated that the RBI might refrain from\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday as they suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Tuesday had failed to stop the rupee hitting its weakest level\par since in over a year.\par     The Karnataka state election that concluded on Tuesday\par delivered a hung parliament with India's ruling BJP emerging as\par the strongest party. The Karnataka elections are the first major\par state election ahead of 2019 general elections.\par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The rupiah weakened to its lowest point in over\par two-and-a-half years at 14,105, a day before a key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy decision. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to hike its benchmark rate for\par the first time since 2014 to support the rupiah and stabilise\par domestic markets, a Reuters poll showed.\par     Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skandinaviska Enskilda\par Banken\f28 \uc2 \f2 , believes the "hike is priced in and markets are watching\par the forward guidance."\par      "If they hike and say that's enough... the rupiah will keep\par weakening," he said. "If they hike and say we are ready to hike\par more, that should help the rupiah stabilize."\par            \par     THAI BAHT \par     Thailand's baht weakened 0.5 percent to 32.08 hours\par ahead of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting that is expected to keep rates\par unchanged to support economic growth amid subdued inflation.\par \par     "Despite inflation picking up to the fastest in more than a\par year... we think Bank of Thailand is still expected to keep\par policy rate unchanged for the time being," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\par     April's annual headline inflation was the highest in 40\par months, but was still at the low end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  target\par range.\par \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0528 GMT                        \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.260     110.34        +0.07\par  Sing dlr                     1.343       1.3446        +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr                   29.859      29.848        -0.04\par  Korean won                   1077.200    1073.8        -0.32\par  Baht                         32.080      31.92         -0.50\par  Peso                         52.330      52.471        +0.27\par  Rupiah                       14105.000   14032         -0.52\par  Rupee                        67.820      68.07         +0.37\par  Ringgit                      3.963       3.954         -0.23\par  Yuan                         6.367       6.3725        +0.08\par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.260     112.67        +2.19\par  Sing dlr                     1.343       1.3373        -0.39\par  Taiwan dlr                   29.859      29.848        -0.04\par  Korean won   