\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Suspected \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  stems rupee's fall\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2018\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Indian rupee unexpectedly gains on strong RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds also gain taking comfort from rupee\par \par \uc2 * Rally at risk as macro risks, high oil weigh (Adds details, quotes, bond level)\par \par \uc2 By Suvashree Choudhury\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 16 (Reuters) - Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second consecutive day stemmed the rupee's fall, three dealers said after seeing heavy dollar selling from the outset of trade on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had weakened to a 16-month closing low of 68.15 per dollar on Tuesday, but after the latest round of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support it had bounced back to 67.80, despite the dollar's strength on international markets. "It looks like RBI is in a mood today," said a senior dealer at a state-run bank, estimating that within the first 10 minutes the RBI might have sold $300 million to $400 million proactively to prevent any sharp fall in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Sharply rising U.S. dollar yields have boosted the dollar on international exchanges, and the rupee was also coming under pressure from firm crude oil prices that will weigh on India's already widening trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers had anticipated that the RBI might refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as it suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday had failed to stop the rupee hitting its weakest level since January 27, 2017.\par \par \uc2 The rupee swung in nearly one percent intraday range on Tuesday, its most volatile day in about a year.\par \par \uc2 "Nobody can understand what the RBI wants to do with the rupee. It says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb volatility but sometimes it allows the rupee to move wildly and sometimes it is holding it with a heavy hand," said another dealer at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Indian bond prices strengthened on the rupee's unexpected recovery.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year benchmark bond yield < stood at 7.88 percent early compared with its previous close of 7.90 percent.\par \par \uc2 However, both \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt traders were doubtful whether the rally in the rupee and Indian bonds would last through the week.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, bond dealers expect the yield on 10-year paper to cross the 8-percent mark, a level unseen since June, 2015, due to inflation concerns.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders also expect the rupee to breach the record low 68.8650 level, last touched on November 24, 2016.\par \par \uc2 "It is quite difficult to sustain the rally given India's weakening macro-economic parameters," said another dealer at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Indian rupee has been the worst performer in the region, losing more than 5 percent so far in 2018 while inflation risks have increased on high oil prices raising the probability of faster hikes in interest rates by the RBI.\par \par \uc2 The trade deficit <INTRD=ECI > widened to $13.72 billion in April from $13.25 billion a year ago and could rise further with India importing 80 percent of its oil needs. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-16T06:00:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180516ee5g006tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
