\par\par \b \uc2 Rupee Keeps Falling -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2018\par 12:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1007 GMT - Fresh declines for the rupee to start the week, helped on by exit polls from elections in the southern Indian state of Karnataka pointing to a hung assembly. Results are due tomorrow, and broker \uc2 Kotak\uc2  says a narrow win for the main opposition won't upset markets much. That as 2 traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  say there's chatter of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupee, which is at fresh 16-month lows in getting toward INR67.50/dollar. India's Sensex was barely higher ahead of the close. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0957 GMT - Sterling rises on Monday on the back of dollar weakness, with GBP/USD up 0.3% at 1.3583, and this week it may go up even further, to between 1.37 and 1.38, if Tuesday's U.K. labor market data are "constructive," ING says. According to a WSJ poll of economists, average earnings for the three months to March are expected to have risen 2.9% in the U.K., compared with a 2.8% rise in the corresponding period. EUR/GBP is up 0.1% at 0.8823. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT - Indian Finance Minister Arun Jaitley, who was being treated for kidney-related problems the past couple months, underwent a successful renal transplant today, said the \uc2 All India Institute of Medical Sciences\uc2  . Jaitley is responsible for formulating policies to prop up the economy. Due to bad health, he canceled participation at key events abroad and was working from home. (rajesh.roy@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT - The euro is rising on Monday on the agreement between Italy's 5-Star Movement and far-right League to form a government. The news isn't likely to boost the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much further, though it does help create a bottom for EUR/USD, says ING. "With the latest positioning data showing net EUR longs stabilising...there are tentative signs of a bottoming out in EUR/USD." EUR/USD has been falling for three weeks up to recently due to broad-based dollar strength. On Monday, EUR/USD is up by 0.4% at 1.1986, also because the dollar is retracing some of its previous gains. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT - Though the ringgit rebounded strongly after initial weakness as Malaysian markets reopened this morning after the election, cracks are "likely to appear in the ruling 4-party coalition, which along with fiscal concerns is likely to keep the ringgit at risk," says Charu Chanana at Continuum Economics. She adds \uc2 Anwar Ibrahim\uc2  poised to become PM is likely to keep markets jittery short-term. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0825 GMT - Bitcoin continues to fall on Monday after 13% of losses last week, mainly due to criticizing comments from billionaires such as Warren Buffet and Bill Gates , and the fact that South Korean's biggest cryptocurrency exchange UPbit had invited guests--prosecutors who raided its offices. According to Factset, bitcoin latest trades down 4% at $8,357. Nasdaq stock exchange Chief Executive \uc2 Adena Friedman\uc2  saying bitcoin could be used as a globalized payment mechanism. Meanwhile, the Winklevoss brothers, founders of the \uc2 Gemini\uc2  crypto exchange, won a patent for a trading system for ETPs tied to cryptocurrencies. Ethereum is also falling, by 5% to $697, and \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  is down 6% at $136. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0824 GMT - The euro is rising on Monday, mainly due to dollar weakness, but also because Italy's 5-Star Movement and far-right League have agreed to form a government. Although there may be concerns about a government made up of anti-establishment parties, this "reduces any lingering risks of another Italian election and ongoing political impasse," says ING. However, "any follow-through to EUR price action should be minimal as we still await further details on policy proposals, the name of Italy's next Prime Minister and key ministerial positions." EUR/USD up 0.3% at 1.1973. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0819 GMT - ING recommends tactically selling the dollar, given that the monetary policy divergence theme is unlikely to be of much benefit for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given "softer" U.S. inflation, while "fears of economic under-performance in the rest of the world look overblown now." ING adds: "As such, we do believe that the theme of MEGA: Make Everyone (else) Great Again - that worked so well at the start of the year in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - will come back in play." EUR/USD is up 0.3% at 1.1977. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to again stand pat Wednesday, with all 9 economists surveyed by WSJ expecting the 1-day repurchase rate to remain at 1.5%, where it's been since April 2015. CPI did rise a more-than-expected 1.1% last month, entering the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1-4% target range for the first time since early 2017. The government has also turned more optimistic about Thailand's economic prospects. \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  , which has penciled in two quarter-point hikes for 2H, says more voices for an increase may emerge this week. One policymaker voted against standing pat on concerns about prolonged monetary accommodation. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT - \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says it suggests selling into any rally in \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds. The 10-year bund yield, which moves inversely to prices, last traded at 0.578%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . Bunds recently "seem stuck in a confined range," with yields oscillating around the 0.55% level, but this could change this week, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. "With euro markets facing a rare holiday-free trading week these lackluster dynamics will be put to the test." With economic data mostly second-tier this week it leaves focus on supply, with Germany, France and Spain all selling bonds later in the week. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0741 GMT - If CPI rises similarly for April to today's reading on wholesale prices, \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to hike as soon as next month, posits \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . Consensus is for an interest-rate move not happening for a year. But with oil prices at 3 1/2-year highs and the rupee sliding, inflation pressures could well intensify. (anant.kala@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT - Recent skittishness in emerging markets generally hasn't stopped \uc2 NagaCorp\uc2  from marketing its debut dollar bond, which would also be Cambodia's first. The Hong Kong-listed company, which owns and operates Phnom Penh's only integrated hotel-casino, is offering 2-year debt at around 9.75% via \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  and \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . The deal, which is available to US investors, will price later today and is said to have caught investor interest. The bonds are likely to be rated the same as the company--some 4-5 steps below investment-grade territory. (manju.dalal@wsj.com; @manjudalalsg)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 14, 2018 06:07 ET (10:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180514ee5e0012m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
