\par\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2018\par 12:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 1010 GMT - China's banking and insurance regulator says it will keep up "high pressure" on violation of laws and regulations through imposition of hefty penalties, according to a statement about a meeting held Monday. The regulator says it still faces severe challenges in minimizing financial risks in the banking and insurance sectors and will rely on a preventive approach. ( grace.zhu@wsj.com )\par \par \uc2 1009 GMT - German first-quarter GDP figures, due Tuesday, are expected to show a sharp slowdown in economic activity, with the annualized growth rate seen down at 1.2% compared with 2.5% in the fourth quarter of 2017, according to a Wall Street Journal poll of 16 economists. A period of cold weather, the flu wave and strikes in the engineering and metals industries contributed to the slowdown, economists say. While some positive payback appears likely in the second quarter, economists say they are increasingly questioning their buoyant full-year GDP forecasts following the wobbly start to 2018. (nina.adam@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT - Fresh declines for the rupee to start the week, helped on by exit polls from elections in the southern Indian state of Karnataka pointing to a hung assembly. Results are due tomorrow, and broker \uc2 Kotak\uc2  says a narrow win for the main opposition won't upset markets much. That as 2 traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  say there's chatter of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupee, which is at fresh 16-month lows in getting toward INR67.50/dollar. India's Sensex was barely higher ahead of the close. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0957 GMT - Sterling rises on Monday on the back of dollar weakness, with GBP/USD up 0.3% at 1.3583, and this week it may go up even further, to between 1.37 and 1.38, if Tuesday's U.K. labor market data are "constructive," ING says. According to a WSJ poll of economists, average earnings for the three months to March are expected to have risen 2.9% in the U.K., compared with a 2.8% rise in the corresponding period. EUR/GBP is up 0.1% at 0.8823. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT - Indian Finance Minister Arun Jaitley, who was being treated for kidney-related problems the past couple months, underwent a successful renal transplant today, said the \uc2 All India Institute of Medical Sciences\uc2  . Jaitley is responsible for formulating policies to prop up the economy. Due to bad health, he canceled participation at key events abroad and was working from home. (rajesh.roy@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT - The euro is rising on Monday on the agreement between Italy's 5-Star Movement and far-right League to form a government. The news isn't likely to boost the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much further, though it does help create a bottom for EUR/USD, says ING. "With the latest positioning data showing net EUR longs stabilising...there are tentative signs of a bottoming out in EUR/USD." EUR/USD has been falling for three weeks up to recently due to broad-based dollar strength. On Monday, EUR/USD is up by 0.4% at 1.1986, also because the dollar is retracing some of its previous gains. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT - Though the ringgit rebounded strongly after initial weakness as Malaysian markets reopened this morning after the election, cracks are "likely to appear in the ruling 4-party coalition, which along with fiscal concerns is likely to keep the ringgit at risk," says Charu Chanana at Continuum Economics. She adds Anwar Ibrahim poised to become PM is likely to keep markets jittery short-term. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0825 GMT - Bitcoin continues to fall on Monday after 13% of losses last week, mainly due to criticizing comments from billionaires such as Warren Buffet and Bill Gates , and the fact that South Korean's biggest cryptocurrency exchange UPbit had invited guests--prosecutors who raided its offices. According to Factset, bitcoin latest trades down 4% at $8,357. Nasdaq stock exchange Chief Executive \uc2 Adena Friedman\uc2  saying bitcoin could be used as a globalized payment mechanism. Meanwhile, the Winklevoss brothers, founders of the \uc2 Gemini\uc2  crypto exchange, won a patent for a trading system for ETPs tied to cryptocurrencies. Ethereum is also falling, by 5% to $697, and \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  is down 6% at $136. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0824 GMT - The euro is rising on Monday, mainly due to dollar weakness, but also because Italy's 5-Star Movement and far-right League have agreed to form a government. Although there may be concerns about a government made up of anti-establishment parties, this "reduces any lingering risks of another Italian election and ongoing political impasse," says ING. However, "any follow-through to EUR price action should be minimal as we still await further details on policy proposals, the name of Italy's next Prime Minister and key ministerial positions." EUR/USD up 0.3% at 1.1973. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0819 GMT - ING recommends tactically selling the dollar, given that the monetary policy divergence theme is unlikely to be of much benefit for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given "softer" U.S. inflation, while "fears of economic under-performance in the rest of the world look overblown now." ING adds: "As such, we do believe that the theme of MEGA: Make Everyone (else) Great Again - that worked so well at the start of the year in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - will come back in play." EUR/USD is up 0.3% at 1.1977. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to again stand pat Wednesday, with all 9 economists surveyed by WSJ expecting the 1-day repurchase rate to remain at 1.5%, where it's been since April 2015. CPI did rise a more-than-expected 1.1% last month, entering the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1-4% target range for the first time since early 2017. The government has also turned more optimistic about Thailand's economic prospects. \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  , which has penciled in two quarter-point hikes for 2H, says more voices for an increase may emerge this week. One policymaker voted against standing pat on concerns about prolonged monetary accommodation. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT Currently trading at $1.3583, the British pound is supported by its rising 50-period moving average at $1.3552 on a 30-min chart. Moreover the 30-minutes RSI stands within its buying area between 50 and 70 and confirms the bullish bias. As a consequence, above the horizontal support at $1.3530, further advance towards May 11 top at $1.3595 is expected. The upside breakout of this threshold will open the way towards the horizontal resistance at $1.3620 and towards May 2 high at $1.3650 in extension. Alternatively, a downside breakout of the horizontal support at $1.3530 would call for a weakness towards May 11 bottom at $1.3500 and towards May 10 low at $1.3465 in extension. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9.] (analysts-europe@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 14, 2018 06:10 ET (10:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180514ee5e00164\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
