\par\par \b \uc2 Insurers to Increase Tier-One Debt Issuance: \uc2 Moody's\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2018\par 13:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1116 GMT - Issuance of tier-one debt by European insurers is likely to increase due to favorable funding conditions and the limits that the European Solvency II capital regime places on issuance of tier-two debt, says \uc2 Moody's\uc2  . The credit-rating agency estimates that the European insurers it rates would need to issue around EUR13 billion ($18.4 billion) of new tier-one debt by late 2026 to maintain current solvency levels. The tier-one debt increase will improve insurers' quality of capital, a credit positive, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says. "While new tier-one debt issuance has so far been modest, we expect it to increase in the next two years," said Benjamin Serra , a \uc2 Moody's\uc2  senior vice-president. (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1114 GMT - If the Russian ruble continues to fall, de-coupling from economic fundamentals and oil prices, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  "may consider selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow down the pace of ruble's depreciation," according to \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . "The \uc2 CBR\uc2  may also pause its monetary policy easing cycle to maintain an attractive interest rate differential," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. However, \uc2 CBR\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  said at this stage there is no threat to Russia's financial stability, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now. The Russian ruble fell to its weakest level against the dollar since December 2016 on Tuesday, with USD/RUB last up nearly 4% at 62.9832. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1055 GMT - Danish HICP inflation fell slightly from 0.5% in February to 0.4% in March, its weakest outturn in nine months. Looking ahead, Capital Econmics expects inflation to creep up over the next few years. "And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to wait for the \uc2 ECB\uc2  [\uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ] to raise interest rates before doing so itself, which on our forecasts implies that the first hike will come in Q3 2019." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1054 GMT - India's plan to sell a 76% stake in national carrier \uc2 Air India\uc2  appear set for a hard landing, with \uc2 Jet Airways\uc2  becoming the latest domestic airline to bow out of the race. Jet's Deputy Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Amit Agarwal\uc2  says "considering the terms of offer and based on our review, we are not participating in the process." Last week, India's largest airline \uc2 IndiGo\uc2  had also dropped out, while \uc2 SpiceJet\uc2  has said it simply does not have enough muscle. Although there is still more than a month left for placing bids, there are few contenders under current terms and conditions.( anant.kala@wsj.com )\par \par \uc2 1053 GMT - Last trading up 0.3% at 131.95, EUR/JPY has broken above the 50-day average at 131.92. This leaves it approaching key chart resistance at the 200-day moving average, currently at 132.16, according to Factset. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  technical analysts say they have exited their long positions on EUR/JPY and that they expect the move to hold the initial test. Resistance above the 200-day moving average comes in at 132.43/47, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts say. Once above there, "133.05/09 would be on the cards together with the 134.25," they say. The euro has come close to, but failed to break above, the 200-day moving average on several days during the last month.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1042 GMT - The Russian ruble continues to fall on Tuesday after new Russian sanctions were imposed on Friday, with USD/RUB up 3.2% at 62.5352, having earlier reached a 16-month high of 63.9210, according to Factset. However, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  makes the point that the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market often "tends to overshoot" in such situations, noting that analysts don't have enough information to judge the true extent of the risks involved. But this doesn't mean that "the move has already happened" and the ruble is "ready to retrace - far from it," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1020 GMT - Credit spreads have two significant drivers which point to movements in opposite directions, says \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  . One driver is equity volatility and the other is bond volatility. The VIX index remains above 20 but European government bond volatility is back down "towards the rock bottom lows," says \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  . This makes valuing euro credit "tough" as they look expensive on equity volatility measures but pretty cheap on bond volatility measures. The VIX index is a measure of stock market expectation of volatility implied by S&P 500 index options. The index is calculated by the \uc2 Chicago Board Options Exchange\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1003 GMT - After a banner year for new contingent convertible bonds, many CoCos will need replacement. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  estimates at least $29 billion issued in all years could be replaced in 2018. The debt, whose genesis dates to the financial crisis, became favored by Chinese lenders last year amid new regulatory-capital requirements. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  -rated Chinese banks sold some $56 billion of CoCos. The amount "may fall slightly in 2018," it adds. Overall, new issuance surged 68% to $113 billion in 2017 as Chinese banks returned to the segment. (manju.dalal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0957 GMT - Just because most analysts don't expect Treasury to name any country a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in the upcoming US report, that doesn't mean the release will be a snooze. India could join Treasury's monitoring list for manipulation, along with longtime members like China. \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, a gauge of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have topped the 2%-of-GDP threshold laid out by Treasury, which means the country now meets 2 of 3 criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, according to ANZ. Watch the findings closely as the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  report could provide legitimacy for trade actions the Trump administration might pursue, says Mitul Kotecha at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  . (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT - March's weak inflation data in Norway strengthen the case for the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  to tighten monetary policy only very slowly. Capital Economics suspects interest rates won't rise until 1Q 2019, later than the bank and investors currently anticipate. CPI-ATE inflation fell to 1.2% from 1.4%, against the consensus and \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  forecasts for a rise to 1.5%. Food inflation rose sharply in March last year due to adverse weather in Europe, and as a result it slowed sharply this year, but this effect was predictable so does not explain the miss, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. "Looking ahead, inflation is likely to rise, but only gradually...capacity utilisation is still low by past standards. And the housing market remains a major risk." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT - If China does depreciate the yuan as part of US-related trade actions, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says that would be even-more damaging for China. That as higher tariffs will already lead to "a deterioration of China's terms of trade," resulting in China having "fewer imports in return for its exports and thus suffer a welfare loss." A "weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make imports even more expensive," the bank adds. Meanwhile, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says depreciation "would raise serious doubts about inflation expectations in Japan and the euro area and would box in the \uc2 ECB\uc2  and BoJ in their attempts to bring asset purchases to an end" or in the BoJ's case scrap its 10-year yield target. It notes when the yuan was devalued in August 2015, the biggest gainers were the yen and euro. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT - German Bunds are the "most expensive and overbought asset we can think of in fixed income," says \uc2 Mark Holman\uc2  , chief executive of \uc2 TwentyFour Asset Management\uc2 , and therefore the asset manager is "extremely wary" of Portuguese assets given how tight they are trading to Bunds. The 10-year German-Portuguese government bond-yield spread is currently 118 basis points, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  ; on the same day in 2017 it was around 360 basis points. Portugal and the whole eurozone periphery has clearly benefited from the broadening economic recovery and the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's asset purchases, "but a spread of 110 bps reflects an amount of optimism around the next stage of European integration that we believe is misplaced," Holman says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 10, 2018 07:16 ET (11:16 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180410ee4a001j8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
