\par\par \b \uc2 Global Equities Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2017\par 10:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering Equities. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT - \uc2 Thyssenkrupp\uc2  leads the DAX after the finalization of a deal to merge its European steel activities with \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2 . \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  believes the combination "will bring significant balance-sheet relief on Thyssenkrupp's side," with the German company transferring EUR4 billion in liabilities into the joint venture, more than the EUR3 billion that the bank had expected. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  thinks the deal has a more-than-90% chance of closing and raises target price for Thyssenkrupp shares to EUR32 from EUR29. Shares trade 3.2% higher at EUR26.05. (marc.navarrogonzalez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0806 GMT - Investing in \uc2 Sembcorp Marine\uc2  is the best way to play the recovery in offshore and marine industry, Nomura says, underscoring the cheap valuation of the Singapore-listed rig builder. That as the company won contracts for building at least 2 compressed gas liquid carriers from Texas-based SeaOne, which Nomura estimates to cost about $150 million each. Still, the investment bank keeps its neutral rating on the stock citing the slow pace of new order flow that may continue to pressure earnings. After rising sharply in the last 2 sessions, the stock is currently flat. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0758 GMT - The famous dots in the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  interest rate statement, which forecast medium-term U.S. rates, will be the center of attention when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes its decision at 1800 GMT Wednesday. "What matters much more for USD is what the Fed signals regarding the expected rate path," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says, adding that "it matters less what the Fed signals for the rest of this year." The market will focus on the extent to which the Fed adjusts its expectations for 2018, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. ING says "the key risk to the dollar is a large enough shift in the distribution of dots translating into a downgrade of median interest rate projections." EUR/USD is up 0.1% at 1.2008. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0750 GMT - China's benchmark equity indexes reversed early losses on Wednesday, with focus turning to smaller cap stocks. The Shanghai Composite and ChiNext finished up 0.3% and 0.7%, respectively, while Shenzhen Composite attained a 5-month closing high with a 0.8% gain. Chip makers were under the spotlight amid rotational buying, with Tongfu Microelectronics, Unigroup Guoxin and 10 others logging limit-up gains. Cyclical stocks such as metals and coal rebounded, and so did recently-listed names, though some banks and insurers underperformed. Galaxy Securities, however, said it has turned cautious on 4Q, and recommends sticking to fundamentals such as consumer stocks and large financials. (john.wu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0731 GMT - Investors are wondering if the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  will try to lower real interest rates to slow the rupee's gains on the back of strong capital inflows. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says it won't and would rather buy dollars to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under its flexible inflation-targeting regime, the RBI may take action to account for the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation on inflation, but not as a move to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  per se, MS says. "As capital flows remain strong, we expect the RBI to respond with further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it says. \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are already at an all-time high of more than $400 billion. (anant.kala@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0730 GMT - Reliance Securities adds its voice to those saying investors should try and take part of \uc2 SBI Life Insurance\uc2 's $1.3 billion IPO, India's biggest debut in 7 years. The deal opened today, with bookbuilding occurring through Friday. The broker highlights the country's low life-insurance penetration, rising income levels and Indians' increased preference for financial assets. SBI is India's fastest-growing private-sector life insurer, and retail investors have a decent chance to participate as 31% of the stock to be sold has been reserved for them. The company will be the second public life insurer in India, joining \uc2 ICICI Pru Life Insurance\uc2 . (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0723 GMT - China's growing demand for telecom infrastructure will fuel Yangtze Optical Fibre's growth, says UOB Kay Hain as it starts coverage at buy even though the stock has surged nearly 70% the past 5 weeks. Yangtze Optical "is one of the best proxies to China's burgeoning investment in wireless and fixed-line communication networks," the bank contends. It forecasts 26% compound annual earnings growth through 2019 for YOF, which rises 1% to HK$27.13. UOB's target is HK$33.70. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 0719 GMT - With slowing daily unit sales, Daiwa says China's year-to-date growth of passenger vehicle remains far behind 2017 forecasts--raising the specter of a year-end price war. As such, the broker recommends selling \uc2 Great Wall Motor\uc2  given likely shrinking margins and weak earnings through 2018. But it's still upbeat on Geely and BYD. Great Wall is up 1.9% today while Geely jumps 5.5% to fresh record highs and BYD pops 13%, hitting levels last seen in 2010. (john.wu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0712 GMT - The dollar could well end the year near current levels at around CNY6.5 before falling a bit further versus the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2018 given an expected weak dollar outlook, says Oxford Economics' Louis Kuijs. While sentiment on the yuan and China's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves has improved markedly, net financial capital outflows remain sizeable. As such, a "material relaxation" of Beijing's policy stance on outflows is unlikely any time soon. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0710 GMT - Oversea-Chinese shareholders may unlock some value if the Singapore bank's insurance unit sells a part of its Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says DBS Vickers. Malaysian authorities plan to strictly implement a 70% foreign-ownership cap on local insurance firms. OCBC's Great Eastern earns 40% of its pretax earnings in Malaysia, the home of 6% of OCBC's overall profit by DBS' estimate. Selling 30% of the Malaysian insurance business would thus have a "minimal" impact on OCBC's overall earnings, DBS adds. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0705 GMT - \uc2 Inditex\uc2  is expected to continue seeing double-digit profit growth over the long-term, says Liberum following a "solid" first half reported earlier today. Future growth should be supported by the Spanish retailer's differentiated business model, best-in-class supply chain, price competitive fashion offer and online growth opportunity, it adds. Liberum says that with shares down 8% over the past three months, it is a good buying opportunity. It maintains its buy recommendation, as well as its target price to EUR41 in light of the company's resilient performance in a tough climate. Shares started trading today at EUR32.10, down 2%. (marc.bisbalarias@dowjones.com; @bamarc)\par \par \uc2 0702 GMT -- An early jump in South Korean stocks quickly turned around today, with the Kospi sitting slightly lower most of the day. As the Kospi fell 0.2% to 2412.20, the electricity/gas sector shed 1.8%. But large caps fared OK, with \uc2 Samsung\uc2  up 0.2% and \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  and \uc2 Hyundai Motors\uc2  each jumping more than 1%. Foreigners sold a net KRW188 billion ($167 million) of stock today while individuals and institutions respectively bought a net KRW86 billion and KRW58 billion. (minsun.lee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 20, 2017 04:10 ET (08:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170920ed9k000o8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
