\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian rupee hits over 2-yr high, foreign lenders sell dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2017\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Indian rupee gains sharply, cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not spotted\par \par \uc2 * Rupee rise triggered by heavy dollar sales by foreign banks\par \par \uc2 * Bonds fall as cenbank policy dashes more rate cut hopes (Updates milestone, background, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Suvashree Choudhury\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 2 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened to its highest in more than two years amid heavy selling of dollars by foreign banks, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to cut interest rates having only a limited impact, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had briefly touched a 15-month low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, though it bounced modestly on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The move in the rupee was magnified as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap broader gains in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, adding they were unsure why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stayed away.\par \par \uc2 The RBI typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks by buying or selling dollars whenever the rupee moves sharply either way.\par \par \uc2 "Today, the lack of buying dollars by RBI has made the rupee fly off," said Sajal Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates at Edelweiss Securities.\par \par \uc2 The rupee rose to as much as 63.59 per dollar, its strongest level since July 22, 2015, from its close of 64.0750 on Tuesday. It ended trade at 63.69.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the RBI decision on Wednesday to cut the repo rate had only a limited impact, given the decision had been widely expected. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said any future action would depend on economic data.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year bond yield rose 2 basis points to 6.46 percent, with some traders saying they were disappointed by the RBI's cautious tone.\par \par \uc2 "The document lacked any guidance. There is no indication of future rate cuts," said a dealer at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 In share markets, the broader NSE index closed down 0.33 percent, while the benchmark \uc2 BSE\uc2  index ended 0.30 percent lower. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Biju Dwarakanath) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-2T13:18:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170802ed8200e8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
