\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee strengthens to 2-year high ahead of RBI decision\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2017\par 10:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 2 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened to its highest in two years amid heavy selling of dollars by foreign banks as markets awaited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on interest rates later on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee rose to as much as 63.7575 per dollar, its strongest level since Aug. 10, 2015, from its close of 64.0750 on Tuesday. Traders estimated foreign banks had sold around $1 billion worth of dollars.\par \par \uc2 The gain in the partially convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was magnified as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders added.\par \par \uc2 The RBI is widely expected to cut the repo rate by 25 basis points to a more than 6-1/2 year low after a recent slump in inflation, with markets primarily focused on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals readiness to ease more. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Rafael Nam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-2T09:44:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170802ed8200a3y\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (india near10 inte